window.DOCS["6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96"]={"id":"6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96","summary":{"title_zh":"卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第十二屆締約方大會（兼締約方會議）決議草案彙編","what":"這份文件彙編了第十二屆卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的各項決議草案，涵蓋遵約、2027–2028 年預算、監測報告、議定書有效性審查、財務機制、生物安全資訊交換所、風險評估、偵測與鑑定、社會經濟因素、現代生物技術立法，以及名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書等議題。草案分別轉錄自各附屬機構與遵約委員會的建議，部分條文仍以方括號標示待協商。","points":["草案第 5 項（遵約）提醒締約方指定國家聯絡點、更新生物安全資訊交換所資料並公布法律措施；並對巴布亞紐幾內亞多次未提交國家報告表示嚴重關切。","草案第 6 項（行政與預算）決定 2027–2028 年度整合工作計畫與預算，秘書處費用由本公約、卡塔赫納議定書與名古屋議定書以 72：15：13 比例分攤；議定書核心預算為整體預算的 15%，但具體金額仍以 XX 表示。","草案第 9 項（財務機制）敦促各締約方在國家預算中編列足夠的生物安全經費，並呼籲已開發國家提供充足、可預測且可取得的財務資源與實物捐助。","草案第 10 項（生物安全資訊交換所）請執行秘書持續維護該交換所，並提供新的國家網站範本與相關培訓。","草案第 13 項（風險評估）在方括號內提議新設一個風險評估特設技術專家小組，並擬定最多兩份額外自願指南，主題包括基因改造藻類、魚類與微生物等；第 14 項則請執行秘書起草數位聚合酶連鎖反應補充章節。","草案第 17 項（責任與補救）歡迎新增一件加入文書，邀請尚未批准的締約方盡快完成批准，並鼓勵捐助者支持相關能力建構。"],"open":["[第 8 項第 14 段：要求尚未完全履行義務的締約方建立措施，是否加上「作為優先事項」（as a matter of priority）]","[第 8 項第 14 段：支援應為「充足、可預測且永續」，或僅為「視情況需要」]","[第 8 項第 6 段：「歡迎」是否加上「with appreciation」]","[第 8 項第 27 段：是否加上前瞻、預防與技術監測等方法]","[第 8 項第 51 段：是否加上風險評估屬國家決定、以及利益衝突管理等文字]","[第 9 項第 7(e) 段：能力建構是否限於國家主導的計畫，以及是否設立「直接」專屬資金管道]","[第 12 項序言：應強調「包容性、透明度與公平性」或「完整性」；第 6 段（已開發國家增加繳款）整段是否保留]","[第 13 項：是否新設特設技術專家小組、增列或刪減指南主題、採用第 3 段或第 3 替代段，以及第 5、8、9、10、12 段的措辭與資料來源]"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p001.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2 Distr.: General 23 September 2026 Original: English"},{"t":"Conference of the Parties to the Convention on"},{"t":"Biological Diversity serving as the meeting of"},{"t":"the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety"},{"t":"Twelfth meeting"},{"t":"Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026"},{"t":"Items 5 to 10 and 12 to 17 of the provisional agenda*"},{"t":"Report of the Compliance Committee                               Review of the effectiveness of processes\nAdministration of the Cartagena Protocol                         under the Convention on Biological\nand budget for the trust funds                                   Diversity and its Protocols\nMonitoring and reporting                                         Risk assessment and risk management of\n                                                                 living modified organisms\nAssessment and review of the effectiveness of the\nCartagena Protocol and midterm evaluation of the                 Detection and identification of living\nimplementation plan and capacity-building action                 modified organisms\nplan for the Protocol                                            Socioeconomic considerations\nMatters related to the financial mechanism and                   National legislation, regulations and\nresources                                                        guidelines on new developments in modern\nOperation and activities of the Biosafety                        biotechnology\nClearing-House                                                   Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary","tb":1},{"t":"Protocol on Liability and Redress"},{"t":"Compilation of draft decisions for the twelfth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena"},{"t":"Protocol on Biosafety"},{"t":"Introduction"},{"t":"The present note contains a compilation of draft decisions for the consideration of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety. The compilation comprises the draft decisions contained in the recommendations from the twenty-seventh meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice and the sixth and seventh meetings of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation and the twentieth and twenty-first meetings of the Compliance Committee under the Protocol, as well as additional elements developed by the Secretariat in the light of, inter alia, previous decisions of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol or recommendations of its subsidiary bodies. The mandates for such additional elements are provided in the documents prepared * CBD/CP/MOP/12/1."}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2\n分發：一般\n2026 年 9 月 23 日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/CP/MOP/12/2<br />\n分發：一般<br />\n2026 年 9 月 23 日<br />\n原文：英文</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議形式召開之\n生物多樣性公約締約方大會\n第十二屆會議\n葉里溫，2026 年 10 月 19–30 日\n臨時議程第 5 至 10 項及第 12 至 17 項*\n遵約委員會報告\n卡塔赫納議定書之行政管理\n以及信託基金預算\n監測與報告\n卡塔赫納議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估\n與財務機制及資源相關事項\n生物安全資訊交換所（Biosafety Clearing-House）之運作與活動","html":"<p>以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議形式召開之<br />\n生物多樣性公約締約方大會<br />\n第十二屆會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026 年 10 月 19–30 日<br />\n臨時議程第 5 至 10 項及第 12 至 17 項*<br />\n遵約委員會報告<br />\n卡塔赫納議定書之行政管理<br />\n以及信託基金預算<br />\n監測與報告<br />\n卡塔赫納議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估<br />\n與財務機制及資源相關事項<br />\n生物安全資訊交換所（Biosafety Clearing-House）之運作與活動</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"生物多樣性公約及其議定書下程序有效性之審查\n基因改造活生物體之風險評估與風險管理\n基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定\n社會經濟考量\n關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南\n名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書（Nagoya–Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress）","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約及其議定書下程序有效性之審查<br />\n基因改造活生物體之風險評估與風險管理<br />\n基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定<br />\n社會經濟考量<br />\n關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南<br />\n名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書（Nagoya–Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress）</p>","en":[8,9,10,11]},{"md":"以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議形式召開之締約方大會第十二屆會議決議草案彙編","html":"<p>以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議形式召開之締約方大會第十二屆會議決議草案彙編</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"引言\n本說明包含決議草案之彙編，供以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議審議。此彙編包含科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構第二十七屆會議、執行附屬機構第六及第七屆會議，以及議定書下遵約委員會第二十及第二十一屆會議之建議中所含之決議草案，以及秘書處根據（除其他外）以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議先前決議或其附屬機構建議所開發之額外要素。此類額外要素之授權載於","html":"<p>引言<br />\n本說明包含決議草案之彙編，供以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議審議。此彙編包含科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構第二十七屆會議、執行附屬機構第六及第七屆會議，以及議定書下遵約委員會第二十及第二十一屆會議之建議中所含之決議草案，以及秘書處根據（除其他外）以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議先前決議或其附屬機構建議所開發之額外要素。此類額外要素之授權載於</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"* CBD/CP/MOP/12/1.","html":"<ul>\n<li>CBD/CP/MOP/12/1.</li>\n</ul>","en":[12]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p002.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"under each relevant agenda item of the present meeting. Items for which no draft decision is envisaged (items 1–4, 11 and 18–20) are also indicated in the compilation, with an explanatory note, for the sake of providing an exhaustive list of items."},{"t":"2/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"本次會議下每一相關議程項目所編製之文件中。對於未預期有決議草案之項目（項目 1–4、11 及 18–20），為提供完整之項目清單，亦於彙編中予以標示，並附上說明。","html":"<p>本次會議下每一相關議程項目所編製之文件中。對於未預期有決議草案之項目（項目 1–4、11 及 18–20），為提供完整之項目清單，亦於彙編中予以標示，並附上說明。</p>","en":[0,1,2]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p003.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Contents"},{"t":"Page"},{"t":"Items 1 to 4 ............................................................................................................................... 4 Item 5.       Report of the Compliance Committee ...................................................................... 5 Item 6.       Administration of the Cartagena Protocol and budget for the trust funds ................ 7"},{"t":"Item 7.       Monitoring and reporting .......................................................................................... 9 Item 8.       Assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol and midterm"},{"t":"evaluation of the implementation plan and capacity-building action plan for the"},{"t":"Protocol ................................................................................................................... 10 Item 9.       Matters related to the financial mechanism and resources ...................................... 16 Item 10. Operation and activities of the Biosafety Clearing-House ...................................... 18 Item 11. Cooperation with international organizations, bodies established under other"},{"t":"conventions, and initiatives ..................................................................................... 19 Item 12. Review of the effectiveness of processes under the Convention on Biological"},{"t":"Diversity and its Protocols ...................................................................................... 20 Item 13. Risk assessment and risk management of living modified organisms .................... 21"},{"t":"Item 14. Detection and identification of living modified organisms..................................... 25 Item 15. Socioeconomic considerations ................................................................................ 27 Item 16. National legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern"},{"t":"biotechnology .......................................................................................................... 28 Item 17. Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress ............ 29"},{"t":"Items 18 to 20 ......................................................................................................................... 31"},{"t":"3/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"目錄\n頁碼","html":"<p>目錄<br />\n頁碼</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"項目 1 至 4 ............................................................................................................................... 4\n項目 5.\n遵約委員會報告 ....................................................................................................................... 5","html":"<p>項目 1 至 4 ............................................................................................................................... 4<br />\n項目 5.<br />\n遵約委員會報告 ....................................................................................................................... 5</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"項目 6.\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之行政管理及信託基金預算 .......................................................... 7","html":"<p>項目 6.<br />\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之行政管理及信託基金預算 .......................................................... 7</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"項目 7.\n監測與報告 ............................................................................................................................... 9","html":"<p>項目 7.<br />\n監測與報告 ............................................................................................................................... 9</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"項目 8.\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估 .......................................................................................................................... 10","html":"<p>項目 8.<br />\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估 .......................................................................................................................... 10</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"項目 9.\n與財務機制及資源相關之事項 .............................................................................................. 16","html":"<p>項目 9.<br />\n與財務機制及資源相關之事項 .............................................................................................. 16</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"項目 10. 生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動 .......................................................................... 18\n項目 11. 與國際組織、依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作 .......................................... 19\n項目 12. 審查《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下各程序之有效性 ...................................... 20\n項目 13. 基因改造活生物體之風險評估與風險管理 .............................................................. 21\n項目 14. 基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定 .............................................................................. 25\n項目 15. 社會經濟考量 ...................................................................................................................... 27\n項目 16. 關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南 .............................................. 28\n項目 17. 名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書 .......................................................... 29\n項目 18 至 20 ......................................................................................................................... 31","html":"<p>項目 10. 生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動 .......................................................................... 18<br />\n項目 11. 與國際組織、依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作 .......................................... 19<br />\n項目 12. 審查《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下各程序之有效性 ...................................... 20<br />\n項目 13. 基因改造活生物體之風險評估與風險管理 .............................................................. 21<br />\n項目 14. 基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定 .............................................................................. 25<br />\n項目 15. 社會經濟考量 ...................................................................................................................... 27<br />\n項目 16. 關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南 .............................................. 28<br />\n項目 17. 名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書 .......................................................... 29<br />\n項目 18 至 20 ......................................................................................................................... 31</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p004.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Items 1 to 4"},{"t":"No draft decisions are envisaged under items 1 to 4, owing to the nature of those items. The actions required on the part of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol for those items are reflected in the annotated provisional agenda."},{"t":"4/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 1 至 4\n由於上述議程項目之性質，第 1 至 4 項預計不擬定決議草案。對於同時擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會而言，針對該等議程項目所需採取之行動，已反映於附註暫定議程中。","html":"<p>項目 1 至 4<br />\n由於上述議程項目之性質，第 1 至 4 項預計不擬定決議草案。對於同時擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會而言，針對該等議程項目所需採取之行動，已反映於附註暫定議程中。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p005.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 5"},{"t":"Report of the Compliance Committee"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/3 (annex I, sect. I, para. 1)."},{"t":"Compliance"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"1.      Notes that a number of Parties have not designated the national focal points, competent national authorities or contact points required under the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety;1"},{"t":"2.     Reminds Parties of their obligation to designate their national focal points for the Cartagena Protocol, in compliance with Article 19 of the Protocol, and of the need to designate their Biosafety Clearing-House national focal points, in accordance with the modalities of operation of the Biosafety Clearing-House, and to keep the information up to date;2"},{"t":"3.       Also reminds Parties of their obligation to make available through the Biosafety Clearing-House the contact details of one or more competent national authorities, in accordance with Article 19 of the Cartagena Protocol, and urges those Parties that have not yet done so to make that information available, as a matter of priority;"},{"t":"4.      Further reminds Parties of their obligation to designate a point of contact for the purposes of receiving notifications under Article 17 of the Cartagena Protocol, and urges those that have not yet done so to make such designations as soon as possible;"},{"t":"5.     Urges Parties that are developing their biosafety regulatory frameworks to expedite their work, recognizing that Parties are required under the Cartagena Protocol to take measures for its implementation and that such measures will contribute to achieving Target 17 of the Kunming- Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, 3 and welcomes the support provided in that regard to several Parties by the United Nations Environment Programme, through its Law and Environment Assistance Platform, and Japan, through the Japan Biodiversity Fund;"},{"t":"6.      Reminds Parties of their obligation to publish their legal measures for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol through the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"7.      Recalls the caution in decision CP-11/1 B of 30 October 2024, and welcomes the funding extended by the Global Environment Facility to the cautioned Parties to prepare their fourth and fifth national reports;"},{"t":"8.      Welcomes the submission of the fourth and fifth national reports by Belize and Libya, which resolves their non-compliance with the reporting obligation;"},{"t":"9.      Expresses grave concern that Papua New Guinea has not submitted its third, fourth or fifth national report;"},{"t":"10.      Requests the Committee to consider possible measures to address the repeated non-compliance of Papua New Guinea with its reporting obligation and make a recommendation in that regard to the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol for consideration at its thirteenth meeting;"},{"t":"1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"2 Decision BS-I/3, annex."},{"t":"3 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"5/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 5\n遵約委員會報告\n以下決議草案係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/3（附件 I，第一節，第 1 段）。","html":"<p>項目 5<br />\n遵約委員會報告<br />\n以下決議草案係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/3（附件 I，第一節，第 1 段）。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"遵約\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會","html":"<p>遵約<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"1. **注意到**若干締約方尚未指定卡塔赫納生物安全議定書所要求的國家聯絡點、國家主管機關或聯絡點；¹","html":"<p>1. <strong>注意到</strong>若干締約方尚未指定卡塔赫納生物安全議定書所要求的國家聯絡點、國家主管機關或聯絡點；¹</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"2. **提醒**締約方依據議定書第 19 條，有義務指定其卡塔赫納議定書國家聯絡點，並依據生物安全資訊交換所之運作模式，有必要指定其生物安全資訊交換所國家聯絡點，並保持資訊更新；²","html":"<p>2. <strong>提醒</strong>締約方依據議定書第 19 條，有義務指定其卡塔赫納議定書國家聯絡點，並依據生物安全資訊交換所之運作模式，有必要指定其生物安全資訊交換所國家聯絡點，並保持資訊更新；²</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"3. **亦提醒**締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書第 19 條，有義務透過生物安全資訊交換所提供一個或多個國家主管機關的聯絡詳情，並**敦促**尚未完成此項工作之締約方將該資訊視為優先事項予以提供；","html":"<p>3. <strong>亦提醒</strong>締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書第 19 條，有義務透過生物安全資訊交換所提供一個或多個國家主管機關的聯絡詳情，並<strong>敦促</strong>尚未完成此項工作之締約方將該資訊視為優先事項予以提供；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"4. **進一步提醒**締約方，為了接收卡塔赫納議定書第 17 條項下之通知，有義務指定一處聯絡點，並**敦促**尚未完成此項工作之締約方盡快進行該等指定；","html":"<p>4. <strong>進一步提醒</strong>締約方，為了接收卡塔赫納議定書第 17 條項下之通知，有義務指定一處聯絡點，並<strong>敦促</strong>尚未完成此項工作之締約方盡快進行該等指定；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"5. **敦促**正在制定其生物安全監管架構之締約方加速其工作，並承認締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書要求必須採取措施以落實該議定書，且該等措施將有助於達成昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 17，³ 並**歡迎**聯合國環境規劃署透過其法律與環境協助平台，以及日本透過日本生物多樣性基金，就此方面向若干締約方提供的支持；","html":"<p>5. <strong>敦促</strong>正在制定其生物安全監管架構之締約方加速其工作，並承認締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書要求必須採取措施以落實該議定書，且該等措施將有助於達成昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 17，³ 並<strong>歡迎</strong>聯合國環境規劃署透過其法律與環境協助平台，以及日本透過日本生物多樣性基金，就此方面向若干締約方提供的支持；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"6. **提醒**締約方，有義務透過生物安全資訊交換所公布其落實卡塔赫納議定書之法律措施；","html":"<p>6. <strong>提醒</strong>締約方，有義務透過生物安全資訊交換所公布其落實卡塔赫納議定書之法律措施；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"7. **回顧** 2024 年 10 月 30 日決議 CP-11/1 B 中之警示，並**歡迎**全球環境基金向受警示之締約方提供資金，以準備其第四及第五份國家報告；","html":"<p>7. <strong>回顧</strong> 2024 年 10 月 30 日決議 CP-11/1 B 中之警示，並<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金向受警示之締約方提供資金，以準備其第四及第五份國家報告；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"8. **歡迎**貝里斯與利比亞提交第四及第五份國家報告，此舉解決了其未履行報告義務之不遵約情形；","html":"<p>8. <strong>歡迎</strong>貝里斯與利比亞提交第四及第五份國家報告，此舉解決了其未履行報告義務之不遵約情形；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"9. **表示嚴重關切**巴布亞紐幾內亞尚未提交其第三、第四或第五份國家報告；","html":"<p>9. <strong>表示嚴重關切</strong>巴布亞紐幾內亞尚未提交其第三、第四或第五份國家報告；</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"10. **請求**委員會考慮可能之措施，以解決巴布亞紐幾內亞重複不履行報告義務之情形，並就此向擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十三屆會議審議；","html":"<p>10. <strong>請求</strong>委員會考慮可能之措施，以解決巴布亞紐幾內亞重複不履行報告義務之情形，並就此向擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十三屆會議審議；</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"¹ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n² Decision BS-I/3, annex.\n³ Decision 15/4, annex.","html":"<p>¹ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.<br />\n² Decision BS-I/3, annex.<br />\n³ Decision 15/4, annex.</p>","en":[16,17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p006.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"11. Encourages Parties facing difficulties complying with one or more obligations under the Cartagena Protocol to seek assistance from the Compliance Committee under the Protocol or the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity.4"},{"t":"4 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"6/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"11. **鼓勵**在履行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》一項或多項義務方面面臨困難的締約方，尋求議定書下之遵約委員會或《生物多樣性公約》秘書處之協助。⁴","html":"<p>11. <strong>鼓勵</strong>在履行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》一項或多項義務方面面臨困難的締約方，尋求議定書下之遵約委員會或《生物多樣性公約》秘書處之協助。⁴</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"⁴ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.","html":"<p>⁴ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.</p>","en":[2,3]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p007.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 6"},{"t":"Administration of the Cartagena Protocol and budget for the trust funds"},{"t":"Elements of the following draft decision have been adapted from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/5. Paragraphs 5 and 6 have been adapted from paragraph 6 of recommendation 6/9 of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation."},{"t":"Administration of the Cartagena Protocol and budget for the trust funds"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling decision CP-11/11 of 6 December 2024,"},{"t":"Having considered the information contained in documents prepared by the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity 5 related to the item on the administration of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety6 and budget for the trust funds on the agenda of its twelfth meeting,7"},{"t":"Welcoming with appreciation the financial contributions from developed country Parties to the special voluntary trust funds to facilitate the participation of Parties and indigenous peoples and local communities in the processes of the Convention and its Protocols,"},{"t":"Recognizing the fiscal constraints on Parties, and noting with concern that the participation of developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and the small island developing States among them, and Parties with economies in transition in meetings held under the Convention and its Protocols has been adversely affected by the lack of predictable and sustainable funding,"},{"t":"1.   Decides to adopt an integrated programme of work and budget for the Convention on Biological Diversity, the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization8 for the biennium 2027–2028;"},{"t":"2.    Also decides to share all costs for secretariat services among the Convention, the Cartagena Protocol and the Nagoya Protocol on a ratio of 72 to 15 to 13 for the biennium 2027–2028;"},{"t":"3.     Approves a core programme budget for the General Trust Fund for the Core Programme Budget for the Cartagena Protocol of XX United States dollars for 2027 and XX dollars for 2028, representing 15 per cent of the integrated budget of XX dollars for 2027 and XX dollars for 2028 for the Convention and its Protocols, for the purposes listed in tables XX and XX below;"},{"t":"4.     Adopts the scale of assessments for the apportionment of expenses for 2027 and 2028, in accordance with the scale of assessments of the United Nations,9 as contained in the annex to the present decision;10"},{"t":"5.     Takes note of the executive summary of the report on the external in-depth functional review of the Secretariat11 and the progress report on the functional review;12"},{"t":"5 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"6 Ibid., vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"7 CBD/CP/MOP/12/4, CBD/CP/MOP/12/5 and CBD/CP/MOP/12/5/Add.1."},{"t":"8 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 3008, No. 30619."},{"t":"9 As contained in General Assembly resolution 79/249."},{"t":"10 See CBD/CP/MOP/12/5, annex, table 2. The scale of assessment will be integrated into the decision after a single scale of"},{"t":"contributions for the Convention and its Protocols has been adopted."},{"t":"11 CBD/SBI/6/10, annex."},{"t":"12 CBD/COP/17/4/Add.4."},{"t":"7/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 6\n卡塔赫納議定書之行政管理及信託基金預算\n下列決議草案之要素已根據文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/5 進行調整。\n第 5 及第 6 段已根據執行附屬機構建議 6/9 之第 6 段進行調整。","html":"<p>項目 6<br />\n卡塔赫納議定書之行政管理及信託基金預算<br />\n下列決議草案之要素已根據文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/5 進行調整。<br />\n第 5 及第 6 段已根據執行附屬機構建議 6/9 之第 6 段進行調整。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"卡塔赫納議定書之行政管理及信託基金預算\n擔任卡塔赫納議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，","html":"<p>卡塔赫納議定書之行政管理及信託基金預算<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**回顧** 2024 年 12 月 6 日之決議 CP-11/11，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong> 2024 年 12 月 6 日之決議 CP-11/11，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**考慮到** 生物多樣性公約秘書處⁵為第十二屆會議議程所準備，與卡塔赫納生物安全議定書⁶之行政管理及信託基金預算議程項目相關之文件中所載資訊，⁷","html":"<p><strong>考慮到</strong> 生物多樣性公約秘書處⁵為第十二屆會議議程所準備，與卡塔赫納生物安全議定書⁶之行政管理及信託基金預算議程項目相關之文件中所載資訊，⁷</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"**歡迎** 並**表示感謝** 已開發國家締約方對特別自願信託基金所提供的財務貢獻，以促進締約方、原住民族與地方社區參與公約及其議定書之程序，","html":"<p><strong>歡迎</strong> 並<strong>表示感謝</strong> 已開發國家締約方對特別自願信託基金所提供的財務貢獻，以促進締約方、原住民族與地方社區參與公約及其議定書之程序，</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**認識到** 締約方面臨的財政限制，並**關切地注意到** 因缺乏可預測且永續的資金，導致開發中國家締約方（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及經濟轉型中締約方在根據公約及其議定書所召開之會議中的參與受到不利影響，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong> 締約方面臨的財政限制，並<strong>關切地注意到</strong> 因缺乏可預測且永續的資金，導致開發中國家締約方（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及經濟轉型中締約方在根據公約及其議定書所召開之會議中的參與受到不利影響，</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1. **決定** 採納生物多樣性公約、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書以及關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享之名古屋議定書⁸ 2027–2028 兩年期之整合工作計畫與預算；","html":"<p>1. <strong>決定</strong> 採納生物多樣性公約、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書以及關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享之名古屋議定書⁸ 2027–2028 兩年期之整合工作計畫與預算；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"2. **亦決定** 在 2027–2028 兩年期內，按 72：15：13 之比例，在公約、卡塔赫納議定書與名古屋議定書之間分攤所有秘書處服務之成本；","html":"<p>2. <strong>亦決定</strong> 在 2027–2028 兩年期內，按 72：15：13 之比例，在公約、卡塔赫納議定書與名古屋議定書之間分攤所有秘書處服務之成本；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"3. **核准** 卡塔赫納議定書核心計畫預算一般信託基金之核心計畫預算，2027 年為 XX 美元，2028 年為 XX 美元，其金額相當於公約及其議定書 2027 年 XX 美元及 2028 年 XX 美元之整合預算之 15%，用於下表 XX 與 XX 所列之用途；","html":"<p>3. <strong>核准</strong> 卡塔赫納議定書核心計畫預算一般信託基金之核心計畫預算，2027 年為 XX 美元，2028 年為 XX 美元，其金額相當於公約及其議定書 2027 年 XX 美元及 2028 年 XX 美元之整合預算之 15%，用於下表 XX 與 XX 所列之用途；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"4. **採納** 2027 年及 2028 年費用分攤之分攤比額表，依據聯合國之分攤比額表⁹，如本決議附件¹⁰所載；","html":"<p>4. <strong>採納</strong> 2027 年及 2028 年費用分攤之分攤比額表，依據聯合國之分攤比額表⁹，如本決議附件¹⁰所載；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"5. **注意到** 秘書處外部深入功能性審查（functional review）報告¹¹之執行摘要及功能性審查進度報告¹²；","html":"<p>5. <strong>注意到</strong> 秘書處外部深入功能性審查（functional review）報告¹¹之執行摘要及功能性審查進度報告¹²；</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"⁵ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n⁶ 同上，vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n⁷ CBD/CP/MOP/12/4, CBD/CP/MOP/12/5 and CBD/CP/MOP/12/5/Add.1.\n⁸ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 3008, No. 30619.\n⁹ 如聯合國大會決議 79/249 所載。\n¹⁰ 見 CBD/CP/MOP/12/5, 附件, 表 2。在採納公約及其議定書之單一分攤率後，該分攤率將併入決議中。\n¹¹ CBD/SBI/6/10, 附件。\n¹² CBD/COP/17/4/Add.4.","html":"<p>⁵ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.<br />\n⁶ 同上，vol. 2226, No. 30619.<br />\n⁷ CBD/CP/MOP/12/4, CBD/CP/MOP/12/5 and CBD/CP/MOP/12/5/Add.1.<br />\n⁸ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 3008, No. 30619.<br />\n⁹ 如聯合國大會決議 79/249 所載。<br />\n¹⁰ 見 CBD/CP/MOP/12/5, 附件, 表 2。在採納公約及其議定書之單一分攤率後，該分攤率將併入決議中。<br />\n¹¹ CBD/SBI/6/10, 附件。<br />\n¹² CBD/COP/17/4/Add.4.</p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p008.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"6.    Decides to apply paragraphs 4, 5 and 7 to 36 of decision 17/-- of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on the administration of the Convention and budget for the trust funds, mutatis mutandis."},{"t":"8/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"6. **決定**在處理公約之行政管理及信託基金預算時，比照適用締約方大會第 17/-- 號決議之第 4、5 及第 7 至 36 段，並進行必要之修正。","html":"<p>6. <strong>決定</strong>在處理公約之行政管理及信託基金預算時，比照適用締約方大會第 17/-- 號決議之第 4、5 及第 7 至 36 段，並進行必要之修正。</p>","en":[0,1,2]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p009.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 7"},{"t":"Monitoring and reporting"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/6."},{"t":"Monitoring and reporting"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling Article 33 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety 13 and its decision CP-10/9 of 10 December 2022, in which it requested Parties to submit to the Secretariat their fifth national reports on the implementation of the Protocol,"},{"t":"1.     Welcomes the fact that more than two thirds of Parties submitted their fifth national reports on the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol by the reporting deadline;"},{"t":"2.      Reminds Parties that have not yet submitted their fifth national reports to do so as soon as possible through the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"3.    Expresses its appreciation to the Global Environment Facility and the United Nations Environment Programme for the support provided to eligible Parties for the preparation and submission of their fifth national reports;"},{"t":"4.      Notes that the sixth national reports will be due by 30 June 2029;"},{"t":"5.     Requests the Executive Secretary to prepare the format for the sixth national report, taking into account the comments provided by Parties in the fifth national reports, while maintaining continuity in the questions in order to facilitate the measurement of progress against the indicators in the implementation plan for the Cartagena Protocol,14 and to submit the format for consideration by the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol at its thirteenth meeting."},{"t":"13 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"14 Decision CP-10/3, annex."},{"t":"9/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 7\n監測與報告\n以下決議草案轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/6。","html":"<p>項目 7<br />\n監測與報告<br />\n以下決議草案轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/6。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"監測與報告\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，","html":"<p>監測與報告<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**回顧**《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 33 條 $^{13}$ 以及其 2022 年 12 月 10 日之決議 CP-10/9，該決議要求締約方將其第五份關於議定書實施情況的國家報告提交予秘書處，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 33 條 <sup>13</sup> 以及其 2022 年 12 月 10 日之決議 CP-10/9，該決議要求締約方將其第五份關於議定書實施情況的國家報告提交予秘書處，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**超過三分之二的締約方已在報告截止日期前提交其第五份關於卡塔赫納生物安全議定書實施情況的國家報告；\n2. **提醒**尚未提交第五份國家報告的締約方，應儘快透過生物安全資訊交換所進行提交；\n3. **對**全球環境基金與聯合國環境規劃署為符合資格的締約方在編製與提交第五份國家報告方面所提供的支持，表示感謝；\n4. **注意到**第六份國家報告的截止日期為 2029 年 6 月 30 日；\n5. **請求**執行秘書考量締約方在第五份國家報告中所提供的意見，編製第六份國家報告的格式，同時維持問題的連續性，以利於衡量卡塔赫納生物安全議定書實施計畫中指標的進展程度，$^{14}$ 並將該格式提交至第十三屆會議的擔任議定書締約方會議的締約方大會供其審議。","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>超過三分之二的締約方已在報告截止日期前提交其第五份關於卡塔赫納生物安全議定書實施情況的國家報告；<br />\n2. <strong>提醒</strong>尚未提交第五份國家報告的締約方，應儘快透過生物安全資訊交換所進行提交；<br />\n3. <strong>對</strong>全球環境基金與聯合國環境規劃署為符合資格的締約方在編製與提交第五份國家報告方面所提供的支持，表示感謝；<br />\n4. <strong>注意到</strong>第六份國家報告的截止日期為 2029 年 6 月 30 日；<br />\n5. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書考量締約方在第五份國家報告中所提供的意見，編製第六份國家報告的格式，同時維持問題的連續性，以利於衡量卡塔赫納生物安全議定書實施計畫中指標的進展程度，<sup>14</sup> 並將該格式提交至第十三屆會議的擔任議定書締約方會議的締約方大會供其審議。</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[11]},{"md":"$^{13}$ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.","html":"<p><sup>13</sup> United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"$^{14}$ Decision CP-10/3, annex.","html":"<p><sup>14</sup> Decision CP-10/3, annex.</p>","en":[12,13]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p010.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 8"},{"t":"Assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"and midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and"},{"t":"capacity-building action plan for the Protocol"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from recommendation 7/5 of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation. Paragraphs 17, 23, 24, 25, 30, 52 and 53 of the draft decision contained in recommendation 7/5 will be considered under item 9 and have been included in the draft decision under that item."},{"t":"Fifth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety and midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the Protocol"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling its decisions CP-10/3 and CP-10/4 of 19 December 2022 and CP-10/7 of 10 December 2022,"},{"t":"Acknowledging with appreciation the analysis of information for the fifth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety15 and midterm evaluation of the implementation plan16 and the capacity-building action plan17 for the Protocol,18"},{"t":"1.     Welcomes the progress made in the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety and towards the achievement of the goals of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the Protocol;"},{"t":"2.     Notes with concern that important gaps persist in areas critical for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol and that biosafety capacity-building and development remain a priority, in particular in risk assessment and risk management and for the detection and identification of living modified organisms;"},{"t":"3.    Recognizes that capacity-building and development and dedicated and predictable resources remain priorities for the effective implementation of the Cartagena Protocol and the successful achievement of the goals of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the Protocol for developing country Parties, in particular the least developed and the small island developing States among them, and Parties with economies in transition;"},{"t":"4.     Calls upon Parties to accelerate their efforts to implement the Cartagena Protocol and use as guidance the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan, as well as the findings from the fifth assessment and review of the Protocol and the midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and capacity-building action plan for the Protocol, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities, capacities and institutional arrangements;"},{"t":"5.    Recognizes the importance of Target 17 of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework19 for furthering the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol, and acknowledges the relevance of the Protocol, its implementation plan and its capacity-building action plan to the achievement of the three objectives of the Convention on Biological Diversity;20"},{"t":"15 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"16 Decision CP-10/3, annex."},{"t":"17 Decision CP-10/4, annex."},{"t":"18 See CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1."},{"t":"19 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"20 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"10/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 8\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估\n下列決議草案係轉載自執行附屬機構之建議 7/5。建議 7/5 中所含之決議草案第 17、23、24、25、30、52 及 53 段將於項目 9 下進行審議，並已包含在該項目之決議草案中。","html":"<p>項目 8<br />\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估<br />\n下列決議草案係轉載自執行附屬機構之建議 7/5。建議 7/5 中所含之決議草案第 17、23、24、25、30、52 及 53 段將於項目 9 下進行審議，並已包含在該項目之決議草案中。</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之第五次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估\n擔任卡塔赫納議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，","html":"<p>卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之第五次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 CP-10/3 與 CP-10/4，以及 2022 年 12 月 10 日之決議 CP-10/7，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 CP-10/3 與 CP-10/4，以及 2022 年 12 月 10 日之決議 CP-10/7，</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**表示讚賞並注意到**針對卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之第五次評估與審查$^{15}$，以及議定書執行計畫$^{16}$與能力建構行動計畫$^{17}$之中期評估$^{18}$，所進行之資訊分析，","html":"<p><strong>表示讚賞並注意到</strong>針對卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之第五次評估與審查<sup>15</sup>，以及議定書執行計畫<sup>16</sup>與能力建構行動計畫<sup>17</sup>之中期評估<sup>18</sup>，所進行之資訊分析，</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**在執行卡塔赫納生物安全議定書，以及朝向達成議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫目標方面所取得之進展；","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>在執行卡塔赫納生物安全議定書，以及朝向達成議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫目標方面所取得之進展；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"2. **表示關切地注意到**在對於執行卡塔赫納議定書至關重要的領域中仍存在重要差距，且生物安全之能力建構與發展仍為優先事項，特別是在風險評估、風險管理，以及基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定方面；","html":"<p>2. <strong>表示關切地注意到</strong>在對於執行卡塔赫納議定書至關重要的領域中仍存在重要差距，且生物安全之能力建構與發展仍為優先事項，特別是在風險評估、風險管理，以及基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定方面；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"3. **認識到**對於開發中國家締約方，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方而言，能力建構與發展，以及專用且可預測之資源，仍是有效執行卡塔赫納議定書，以及成功達成議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫目標之優先事項；","html":"<p>3. <strong>認識到</strong>對於開發中國家締約方，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方而言，能力建構與發展，以及專用且可預測之資源，仍是有效執行卡塔赫納議定書，以及成功達成議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫目標之優先事項；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"4. **呼籲**締約方應根據國家情況、優先事項、能力與制度安排，加速其執行卡塔赫納議定書之努力，並以執行計畫、能力建構行動計畫，以及議定書第五次評估與審查、議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫中期評估之結果作為指引；","html":"<p>4. <strong>呼籲</strong>締約方應根據國家情況、優先事項、能力與制度安排，加速其執行卡塔赫納議定書之努力，並以執行計畫、能力建構行動計畫，以及議定書第五次評估與審查、議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫中期評估之結果作為指引；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"5. **認識到**《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》目標 17$^{19}$對於推進卡塔赫納議定書執行之重要性，並**承認**該議定書、其執行計畫及其能力建構行動計畫，對於達成《生物多樣性公約》三項目標之相關性；$^{20}$","html":"<p>5. <strong>認識到</strong>《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》目標 17<sup>19</sup>對於推進卡塔赫納議定書執行之重要性，並<strong>承認</strong>該議定書、其執行計畫及其能力建構行動計畫，對於達成《生物多樣性公約》三項目標之相關性；<sup>20</sup></p>","en":[13]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[13]},{"md":"$^{15}$ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.","html":"<p><sup>15</sup> United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"$^{16}$ Decision CP-10/3, annex.","html":"<p><sup>16</sup> Decision CP-10/3, annex.</p>","en":[14,15]},{"md":"$^{17}$ Decision CP-10/4, annex.","html":"<p><sup>17</sup> Decision CP-10/4, annex.</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"$^{18}$ See CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1.","html":"<p><sup>18</sup> See CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1.</p>","en":[17]},{"md":"$^{19}$ Decision 15/4, annex.","html":"<p><sup>19</sup> Decision 15/4, annex.</p>","en":[18]},{"md":"$^{20}$ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.","html":"<p><sup>20</sup> United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.</p>","en":[19,20]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p011.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"6.    Welcomes [with appreciation] the global report on collective progress in the implementation of the Framework, in particular the conclusions and key messages relating to the goals and targets of the Framework that are relevant to biosafety, and stresses that adequate support for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol is essential for the achievement of Target 17 of the Framework;"},{"t":"7.    Recognizes the need for complementary and non-duplicative efforts towards the fulfilment of the implementation plan for the Cartagena Protocol and the achievement of the goals and targets of the Framework that are relevant to biosafety;"},{"t":"8.     Urges Parties to the Convention that are also Parties to the Cartagena Protocol to advance efforts to attain the goals and targets of the Framework that are relevant to biosafety, including through the integration of biosafety into national biodiversity strategies and action plans, as appropriate and in accordance with their national circumstances, priorities and existing institutional arrangements;"},{"t":"9.    Welcomes the contributions of the Compliance Committee under the Cartagena Protocol and the Liaison Group on the Cartagena Protocol to the fifth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Protocol and the midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the Protocol;"},{"t":"10. Requests the Compliance Committee and the Liaison Group to provide input to the sixth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol and the final evaluation of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the Protocol;"},{"t":"11. Requests the Liaison Group to consider ways and methodologies to collect and analyse qualitative data in addition to the primarily quantitative information from the national reports, with a view to providing a more complete data set for the sixth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol and the final evaluation of its implementation plan and capacity-building action plan;"},{"t":"Goal A.1: Parties have in place functional national biosafety frameworks21"},{"t":"12. Notes with appreciation the progress made by Parties in designating competent national authorities, but expresses concern that a small number of Parties have still not designated their competent national authorities, and urges them to do so as soon as possible;"},{"t":"13. Expresses concern that several Parties have not taken any measures or have only draft or temporary measures for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"14. Requests Parties that have not yet fully done so to put in place[, as a matter of priority,] legal, administrative and other measures to implement their obligations under the Cartagena Protocol, while acknowledging that Parties face various challenges that prevent them from fully complying with the obligations under Article 2, paragraph 1, of the Protocol, and that institutional, technical, technological and financial support [that is adequate, predictable and sustainable needs to be made available to enable them to fully discharge their commitments under the Protocol][, as appropriate, is needed to support them in this regard];"},{"t":"15. Urges Parties to ensure sufficient biosafety staffing levels for functional national biosafety frameworks;"},{"t":"16. Encourages Parties and other stakeholders to focus capacity-building and development in the context of Goal A.1 of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan on the elaboration of national measures, in particular legislative measures, for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol and on strengthening the capacity of national staff to carry out their functions in the field of biosafety, in accordance with national needs and priorities;"},{"t":"21 Paragraphs 12 to 52 are grouped by the relevant goal of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the"},{"t":"Cartagena Protocol."},{"t":"11/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"6. **歡迎** [並表示讚賞] 關於執行綱要集體進展的全球報告，特別是與生物安全相關之綱要目標與目標的結論及關鍵訊息，並強調為達成綱要目標 17，為執行卡塔赫納議定書提供適當支援至關重要；\n7. **認識到** 為了履行卡塔赫納議定書執行計畫，並達成與生物安全相關之綱要目標與目標，需要採取互補且不重複的努力；\n8. **敦促** 同為卡塔赫納議定書締約方的公約締約方，應推進達成與生物安全相關之綱要目標與目標的努力，包括在適當情況下，並根據其國情、優先事項及現有制度安排，將生物安全納入國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫；\n9. **歡迎** 卡塔赫納議定書下之遵約委員會以及卡塔赫納議定書聯絡小組，對於議定書有效性第五次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估所做出的貢獻；\n10. **請求** 遵約委員會與聯絡小組，為卡塔赫納議定書有效性的第六次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫的最終評估提供投入；\n11. **請求** 聯絡小組考慮除了來自國家報告的主要量化資訊外，收集與分析質性資料的方法與技術，旨在為卡塔赫納議定書有效性的第六次評估與審查，以及其執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫的最終評估提供更完整的資料集；","html":"<p>6. <strong>歡迎</strong> [並表示讚賞] 關於執行綱要集體進展的全球報告，特別是與生物安全相關之綱要目標與目標的結論及關鍵訊息，並強調為達成綱要目標 17，為執行卡塔赫納議定書提供適當支援至關重要；<br />\n7. <strong>認識到</strong> 為了履行卡塔赫納議定書執行計畫，並達成與生物安全相關之綱要目標與目標，需要採取互補且不重複的努力；<br />\n8. <strong>敦促</strong> 同為卡塔赫納議定書締約方的公約締約方，應推進達成與生物安全相關之綱要目標與目標的努力，包括在適當情況下，並根據其國情、優先事項及現有制度安排，將生物安全納入國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫；<br />\n9. <strong>歡迎</strong> 卡塔赫納議定書下之遵約委員會以及卡塔赫納議定書聯絡小組，對於議定書有效性第五次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估所做出的貢獻；<br />\n10. <strong>請求</strong> 遵約委員會與聯絡小組，為卡塔赫納議定書有效性的第六次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫的最終評估提供投入；<br />\n11. <strong>請求</strong> 聯絡小組考慮除了來自國家報告的主要量化資訊外，收集與分析質性資料的方法與技術，旨在為卡塔赫納議定書有效性的第六次評估與審查，以及其執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫的最終評估提供更完整的資料集；</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"長期目標 A.1：締約方已建立具功能性的國家生物安全框架$^{21}$","html":"<p>長期目標 A.1：締約方已建立具功能性的國家生物安全框架<sup>21</sup></p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"12. **表示讚賞地注意到** 締約方在指定國家主管機關方面所取得的進展，但表示關切仍有少數締約方尚未指定其國家主管機關，並敦促其盡快完成指定；\n13. **表示關切** 若干締約方尚未採取任何措施，或僅針對卡塔赫納議定書的執行採取草案或臨時性措施；\n14. **請求** 尚未完全做到此事的締約方，[作為優先事項，] 建立法律、行政及其他措施以履行其在卡塔赫納議定書下的義務，同時承認締約方面臨各種挑戰，阻礙其完全履行議定書第二條第一項下的義務，且[需要提供適當、可預測且永續的制度、技術、科技與財務支援，以使其能夠充分履行其在議定書下的承諾][，在適當情況下，需要以此支持其在此方面的努力]；\n15. **敦促** 締約方確保國家生物安全框架具備充足的生物安全人員配置；\n16. **鼓勵** 締約方及其他利害關係人，在執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之長期目標 A.1 的背景下，根據國家需求與優先事項，將能力建構與發展重點放在制定執行卡塔赫納議定書的國家措施（特別是立法措施），以及強化國家人員在生物安全領域執行職能的能力；","html":"<p>12. <strong>表示讚賞地注意到</strong> 締約方在指定國家主管機關方面所取得的進展，但表示關切仍有少數締約方尚未指定其國家主管機關，並敦促其盡快完成指定；<br />\n13. <strong>表示關切</strong> 若干締約方尚未採取任何措施，或僅針對卡塔赫納議定書的執行採取草案或臨時性措施；<br />\n14. <strong>請求</strong> 尚未完全做到此事的締約方，[作為優先事項，] 建立法律、行政及其他措施以履行其在卡塔赫納議定書下的義務，同時承認締約方面臨各種挑戰，阻礙其完全履行議定書第二條第一項下的義務，且[需要提供適當、可預測且永續的制度、技術、科技與財務支援，以使其能夠充分履行其在議定書下的承諾][，在適當情況下，需要以此支持其在此方面的努力]；<br />\n15. <strong>敦促</strong> 締約方確保國家生物安全框架具備充足的生物安全人員配置；<br />\n16. <strong>鼓勵</strong> 締約方及其他利害關係人，在執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之長期目標 A.1 的背景下，根據國家需求與優先事項，將能力建構與發展重點放在制定執行卡塔赫納議定書的國家措施（特別是立法措施），以及強化國家人員在生物安全領域執行職能的能力；</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"$^{21}$ 第 12 至 52 段依據卡塔赫納議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之相關目標進行分組。","html":"<p><sup>21</sup> 第 12 至 52 段依據卡塔赫納議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之相關目標進行分組。</p>","en":[13,14,15]}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p012.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Goal A.2: Parties have improved the availability and exchange of relevant information through the Biosafety Clearing-House"},{"t":"17. Welcomes progress towards Goal A.2 of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan, in particular the increase in the number of Parties publishing mandatory information, as well as the increase in the number of active users of and visits to the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"18. Recognizes that the launch of the new platform of the Biosafety Clearing-House and the help materials developed and capacity-building activities undertaken by the Secretariat have contributed positively to the increase in the use of the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"19. Urges Parties that have not yet fully done so to make all required information available through the Biosafety Clearing-House and keep their records up to date;"},{"t":"20. Requests the Executive Secretary to continue to provide support for maintaining the Biosafety Clearing-House as the principal mechanism for sharing information under the Cartagena Protocol, in particular by continuing to provide capacity-building and development activities and training to Parties, developing user-friendly and accessible digital tools and promoting the interoperability of existing databases and information systems;"},{"t":"21. Encourages Parties, and invites relevant organizations, to provide support for the implementation by Parties of the provisions of the Cartagena Protocol related to information-sharing and for the effective use of the Biosafety Clearing-House by strengthening national capacities for biosafety information management, improving the quality, completeness, accuracy and timeliness of information submitted by Parties and promoting technical cooperation and knowledge exchange; Goal A.3: full information on the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol is made available by Parties in a timely manner"},{"t":"Goal A.4: Parties are in compliance with the requirements of the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"22. Welcomes progress made by Parties in complying with their obligations under the Cartagena Protocol, notably those concerning the submission of national reports and the publishing of information through the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"23. Also welcomes the high rate of compliance with the obligation to designate national focal points;"},{"t":"24. Further welcomes the supportive role of the Compliance Committee, and acknowledges the importance of its regular follow-up with Parties on compliance matters and the formal compliance measures and informal efforts of the Compliance Committee in support of compliance and the achievement of Goal A.4 of the implementation plan for the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"25. Requests Parties to cooperate fully when receiving communications from the Compliance Committee;"},{"t":"Goal A.5: Parties carry out scientifically sound risk assessments of living modified organisms and manage and control identified risks to prevent adverse effects of living modified organisms on the conservation and sustainable use of biological diversity, taking also into account risks to human health"},{"t":"26. Recognizes that conducting risk assessment and risk management continues to pose challenges for some Parties and that those challenges are made more difficult by the rapidity of developments in modern biotechnology, including the application of synthetic biology and other new genetic modification techniques for the development of living modified organisms, in particular when evaluating potential adverse effects in complex receiving environments;"},{"t":"27. Also recognizes that rapid developments in modern biotechnology require the continuous updating of relevant scientific, technical and institutional capacities[, including, as"},{"t":"12/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"長期目標 A.2：締約方已透過生物安全資訊交換所，改善相關資訊的可取得性與交換\n17. **歡迎**執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫在達成長期目標 A.2 方面的進展，特別是發布強制性資訊的締約方數量增加，以及生物安全資訊交換所的使用者數量與造訪次數增加；\n18. **注意到**生物安全資訊交換所新平台的啟動，以及秘書處所開發的協助材料與開展的能力建構活動，對於增加生物安全資訊交換所的使用量具有正面貢獻；\n19. **敦促**尚未完全落實的締約方，應透過生物安全資訊交換所提供所有要求的資訊，並保持其紀錄之更新；\n20. **請求**執行秘書繼續提供支持，以維護生物安全資訊交換所作為《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》下分享資訊的主要機制，特別是透過繼續為締約方提供能力建構與發展活動及培訓，開發使用者友善且易於取得的數位工具，並促進現有資料庫與資訊系統的互通性；\n21. **鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**相關組織，透過強化生物安全資訊管理之國家能力、提高締約方提交資訊的品質、完整性、準確性與及時性，以及促進技術合作與知識交換，為締約方履行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》中與資訊分享相關之規定，以及有效使用生物安全資訊交換所提供支持；","html":"<p>長期目標 A.2：締約方已透過生物安全資訊交換所，改善相關資訊的可取得性與交換<br />\n17. <strong>歡迎</strong>執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫在達成長期目標 A.2 方面的進展，特別是發布強制性資訊的締約方數量增加，以及生物安全資訊交換所的使用者數量與造訪次數增加；<br />\n18. <strong>注意到</strong>生物安全資訊交換所新平台的啟動，以及秘書處所開發的協助材料與開展的能力建構活動，對於增加生物安全資訊交換所的使用量具有正面貢獻；<br />\n19. <strong>敦促</strong>尚未完全落實的締約方，應透過生物安全資訊交換所提供所有要求的資訊，並保持其紀錄之更新；<br />\n20. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書繼續提供支持，以維護生物安全資訊交換所作為《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》下分享資訊的主要機制，特別是透過繼續為締約方提供能力建構與發展活動及培訓，開發使用者友善且易於取得的數位工具，並促進現有資料庫與資訊系統的互通性；<br />\n21. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>相關組織，透過強化生物安全資訊管理之國家能力、提高締約方提交資訊的品質、完整性、準確性與及時性，以及促進技術合作與知識交換，為締約方履行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》中與資訊分享相關之規定，以及有效使用生物安全資訊交換所提供支持；</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"長期目標 A.3：締約方及時提供關於履行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之完整資訊\n長期目標 A.4：締約方符合《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之要求\n22. **歡迎**締約方在履行其《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》義務方面所取得的進展，特別是關於提交國家報告以及透過生物安全資訊交換所發布資訊之義務；\n23. **亦歡迎**指定國家聯絡點之義務具有高水平的遵約率；\n24. **進一步歡迎**遵約委員會的支持作用，並承認其定期就遵約事項與締約方進行後續追蹤的重要性，以及遵約委員會為支持遵約及達成《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》執行計畫長期目標 A.4 所採取的正式遵約措施與非正式努力；\n25. **請求**締約方在收到遵約委員會之通訊時應充分合作；","html":"<p>長期目標 A.3：締約方及時提供關於履行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之完整資訊<br />\n長期目標 A.4：締約方符合《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之要求<br />\n22. <strong>歡迎</strong>締約方在履行其《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》義務方面所取得的進展，特別是關於提交國家報告以及透過生物安全資訊交換所發布資訊之義務；<br />\n23. <strong>亦歡迎</strong>指定國家聯絡點之義務具有高水平的遵約率；<br />\n24. <strong>進一步歡迎</strong>遵約委員會的支持作用，並承認其定期就遵約事項與締約方進行後續追蹤的重要性，以及遵約委員會為支持遵約及達成《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》執行計畫長期目標 A.4 所採取的正式遵約措施與非正式努力；<br />\n25. <strong>請求</strong>締約方在收到遵約委員會之通訊時應充分合作；</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"長期目標 A.5：締約方對基因改造活生物體進行科學上健全的風險評估，並管理與控制已識別之風險，以防止基因改造活生物體對生物多樣性保育與永續利用產生不利影響，並同時考慮對人類健康的風險\n26. **注意到**進行風險評估與風險管理對某些締約方而言仍持續面臨挑戰，且由於現代生物技術發展迅速（包括應用合成生物學及其他新基因改造技術來開發基因改造活生物體），使得這些挑戰更加困難，特別是在評估複雜接收環境中的潛在不利影響時；\n27. **亦注意到**現代生物技術的快速發展，需要持續更新相關的科學、技術及制度能力[, 包括，作為","html":"<p>長期目標 A.5：締約方對基因改造活生物體進行科學上健全的風險評估，並管理與控制已識別之風險，以防止基因改造活生物體對生物多樣性保育與永續利用產生不利影響，並同時考慮對人類健康的風險<br />\n26. <strong>注意到</strong>進行風險評估與風險管理對某些締約方而言仍持續面臨挑戰，且由於現代生物技術發展迅速（包括應用合成生物學及其他新基因改造技術來開發基因改造活生物體），使得這些挑戰更加困難，特別是在評估複雜接收環境中的潛在不利影響時；<br />\n27. <strong>亦注意到</strong>現代生物技術的快速發展，需要持續更新相關的科學、技術及制度能力[, 包括，作為</p>","en":[11,12,13,14,15]}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p013.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"appropriate, through forward-looking and precautionary approaches, horizon scanning and technology monitoring to support national preparedness and informed decision-making];"},{"t":"28. Encourages Parties and other stakeholders to continue to address human resource, financing and infrastructure needs concerning the key areas for capacity-building related to risk assessment and risk management in the capacity-building action plan;"},{"t":"29. Encourages Parties and relevant organizations to establish regional networks of risk assessment and risk management experts to facilitate peer review, technical support and knowledge exchange among Parties, including with the support of the regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres;"},{"t":"Goal A.6: Parties prevent and address illegal and unintentional transboundary movements of living modified organisms"},{"t":"30. Reminds Parties to report cases of illegal and unintentional transboundary movements through the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"31. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to provide support for capacity-building and development on preventing and addressing illegal and unintentional transboundary movements of living modified organisms, with a particular focus on addressing challenges related to limited laboratory detection capacities, insufficient laboratory equipment and infrastructure, insufficiently trained personnel, porous borders and institutional and regulatory gaps; Goal A.7: Parties have measures in place to fulfil the handling, transport, packaging and identification requirements of living modified organisms under Article 18 of the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"32. Encourages Parties to facilitate cross-sectoral cooperation and coordination among competent national biosafety authorities, customs authorities and other relevant government bodies to strengthen capacity for the handling, transport, packaging and identification of living modified organisms;"},{"t":"33. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to provide support for capacity-building and development on fulfilling the handling, packaging and identification requirements for living modified organisms, with a particular focus on addressing challenges related to: the operationalization of legal frameworks; the training of customs officers; and access to adequate facilities, equipment and resources for the detection and identification of living modified organisms, including through technology transfer and the strengthening of technical support at the national level;"},{"t":"Goal A.8: Parties are able to detect and identify living modified organisms"},{"t":"34. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to provide support for capacity-building and development in the areas of detection and identification of living modified organisms, with a particular focus on addressing challenges related to limited access to accredited laboratories, certified reference materials, especially for newly commercialized living modified organisms, validated detection methods, adequate equipment, sustainable financial resources and sufficient trained personnel;"},{"t":"35. Calls for enhanced technology transfer and technical cooperation to strengthen national and regional capacities for the detection, identification and monitoring of living modified organisms; Goal A.9: Parties that choose to do so take into account socioeconomic considerations when making decisions on the import of living modified organisms and cooperate on research and information exchange, in accordance with Article 26 of the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"36. Acknowledges that regulatory frameworks for enabling the consideration of socioeconomic aspects, as well as the assessment of socioeconomic impacts, remain challenges for Parties that choose to take into account socioeconomic considerations when making decisions on the"},{"t":"13/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"[適當時，透過前瞻性與預防性方法、水平掃描及技術監測，以支持國家準備工作與知情決策]；\n28. **鼓勵**締約方與其他利害關係人，在與風險評估及風險管理相關之能力建構行動計畫中，持續應對有關能力建構關鍵領域的人力資源、財務及基礎設施需求；\n29. **鼓勵**締約方與相關組織建立風險評估與風險管理專家之區域網絡，以促進締約方之間的同儕審查、技術支援與知識交換，包括在區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心的協助下進行；","html":"<p>[適當時，透過前瞻性與預防性方法、水平掃描及技術監測，以支持國家準備工作與知情決策]；<br />\n28. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方與其他利害關係人，在與風險評估及風險管理相關之能力建構行動計畫中，持續應對有關能力建構關鍵領域的人力資源、財務及基礎設施需求；<br />\n29. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方與相關組織建立風險評估與風險管理專家之區域網絡，以促進締約方之間的同儕審查、技術支援與知識交換，包括在區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心的協助下進行；</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"長期目標 A.6：締約方防止並應對基因改造活生物體非法且非故意之跨境移動","html":"<p>長期目標 A.6：締約方防止並應對基因改造活生物體非法且非故意之跨境移動</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"30. **提醒**締約方應透過生物安全資訊交換所通報非法且非故意之跨境移動案例；\n31. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，針對防止與應對基因改造活生物體非法且非故意之跨境移動，提供能力建構與發展之支援，並特別著重於應對與實驗室檢測能力有限、實驗室設備與基礎設施不足、人員培訓不足、邊境管控薄弱以及制度與監管落差相關之挑戰；","html":"<p>30. <strong>提醒</strong>締約方應透過生物安全資訊交換所通報非法且非故意之跨境移動案例；<br />\n31. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，針對防止與應對基因改造活生物體非法且非故意之跨境移動，提供能力建構與發展之支援，並特別著重於應對與實驗室檢測能力有限、實驗室設備與基礎設施不足、人員培訓不足、邊境管控薄弱以及制度與監管落差相關之挑戰；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"長期目標 A.7：締約方已具備相關措施，以符合《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 18 條下基因改造活生物體之處理、運輸、包裝與識別要求","html":"<p>長期目標 A.7：締約方已具備相關措施，以符合《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 18 條下基因改造活生物體之處理、運輸、包裝與識別要求</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"32. **鼓勵**締約方促進國家生物安全主管機關、海關主管機關及其他相關政府部門之間的跨部門合作與協調，以強化基因改造活生物體之處理、運輸、包裝與識別能力；\n33. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，針對符合基因改造活生物體之處理、包裝與識別要求，提供能力建構與發展之支援，並特別著重於應對與下列事項相關之挑戰：法律框架的落實；海關人員之培訓；以及取得足夠之設施、設備與資源以進行基因改造活生物體之檢測與識別，包括透過技術轉移及強化國家層級之技術支援；","html":"<p>32. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方促進國家生物安全主管機關、海關主管機關及其他相關政府部門之間的跨部門合作與協調，以強化基因改造活生物體之處理、運輸、包裝與識別能力；<br />\n33. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，針對符合基因改造活生物體之處理、包裝與識別要求，提供能力建構與發展之支援，並特別著重於應對與下列事項相關之挑戰：法律框架的落實；海關人員之培訓；以及取得足夠之設施、設備與資源以進行基因改造活生物體之檢測與識別，包括透過技術轉移及強化國家層級之技術支援；</p>","en":[7,8]},{"md":"長期目標 A.8：締約方能夠檢測並識別基因改造活生物體","html":"<p>長期目標 A.8：締約方能夠檢測並識別基因改造活生物體</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"34. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，針對基因改造活生物體檢測與識別領域，提供能力建構與發展之支援，並特別著重於應對與下列事項相關之挑戰：取得認可實驗室與認證標準物質之機會有限（特別是針對新上市之基因改造活生物體）、經驗證之檢測方法、足夠之設備、永續之財務資源以及充足之受訓人員；\n35. **呼籲**加強技術轉移與技術合作，以強化國家與區域在基因改造活生物體檢測、識別與監測方面之能力；","html":"<p>34. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，針對基因改造活生物體檢測與識別領域，提供能力建構與發展之支援，並特別著重於應對與下列事項相關之挑戰：取得認可實驗室與認證標準物質之機會有限（特別是針對新上市之基因改造活生物體）、經驗證之檢測方法、足夠之設備、永續之財務資源以及充足之受訓人員；<br />\n35. <strong>呼籲</strong>加強技術轉移與技術合作，以強化國家與區域在基因改造活生物體檢測、識別與監測方面之能力；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"長期目標 A.9：選擇如此做之締約方，在對基因改造活生物體之進口做出決策時，應考慮社會經濟因素，並根據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 26 條，在研究與資訊交換方面進行合作","html":"<p>長期目標 A.9：選擇如此做之締約方，在對基因改造活生物體之進口做出決策時，應考慮社會經濟因素，並根據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 26 條，在研究與資訊交換方面進行合作</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"36. **承認**旨在使社會經濟層面得以被納入考量之監管框架，以及社會經濟影響評估，對於選擇在對基因改造活生物體之進口做出決策時","html":"<p>36. <strong>承認</strong>旨在使社會經濟層面得以被納入考量之監管框架，以及社會經濟影響評估，對於選擇在對基因改造活生物體之進口做出決策時</p>","en":[12,13]}]},{"p":"p014","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p014.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"import of living modified organisms, in accordance with Article 26, paragraph 1, of the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"37. Encourages Parties, in accordance with Article 26, paragraph 2, of the Cartagena Protocol, to cooperate on research and information exchange on any socioeconomic impacts of living modified organisms, especially on indigenous peoples and local communities and, among other things, their livelihoods, food systems, traditional agricultural practices and biocultural richness; Goal A.10: Parties to the Cartagena Protocol become Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress and have in place measures to fulfil their obligations under the Supplementary Protocol"},{"t":"38. Encourages Parties to the Cartagena Protocol to accede, ratify, accept or approve, as appropriate, the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress to the Cartagena Protocol;22"},{"t":"39. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to disseminate information on, and promote outreach and awareness-raising about, the Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress among Parties, indigenous peoples and local communities and relevant stakeholders using, where feasible, the languages of indigenous peoples and local communities; Goal B.1: Parties engage in capacity-building activities"},{"t":"40. Calls upon Parties and relevant organizations to facilitate capacity-building and development, taking into account nationally identified needs and priorities and the findings of the fifth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol and the midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan, in the areas in which capacity needs remain most prevalent, namely:"},{"t":"(a)      Risk assessment, risk management and other scientific and technical expertise;"},{"t":"(b)      Sampling, detection and identification;"},{"t":"(c)      Institutional capacity and human resources;"},{"t":"(d)      Public awareness, education and participation;"},{"t":"(e)      Monitoring and reporting;"},{"t":"41. Encourages Parties to cooperate with one another in strengthening capacities for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol, including by involving indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and relevant stakeholders, with emphasis on the needs of developing country Parties, in particular the least developed and the small island developing States among them, and Parties with economies in transition;"},{"t":"42. Invites the technical and scientific cooperation support centres to incorporate biosafety into their biennial workplans and to serve as hubs for biosafety capacity-building and development, information-sharing and North-South, South-South and triangular cooperation;"},{"t":"43. Calls upon relevant organizations, and invites the technical and scientific cooperation support centres, to assist Parties in the development of biosafety project proposals;"},{"t":"44.      Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources:"},{"t":"(a) To continue to undertake capacity-building and development activities to assist Parties in implementing the Cartagena Protocol, and to draw attention periodically to the extensive capacity-building materials available on the Secretariat website;23"},{"t":"22 Decision BS-V/11, annex."},{"t":"23 https://bch.cbd.int/protocol."},{"t":"14/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"考慮社會經濟因素之締約方而言，仍屬挑戰，依據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 26 條第 1 項；\n37. **鼓勵**締約方根據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 26 條第 2 項，針對基因改造活生物體對任何社會經濟影響，特別是對原住民族與地方社區及其生計、食物系統、傳統農業實踐與生物文化豐富度等方面，進行研究與資訊交換之合作；","html":"<p>考慮社會經濟因素之締約方而言，仍屬挑戰，依據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 26 條第 1 項；<br />\n37. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方根據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 26 條第 2 項，針對基因改造活生物體對任何社會經濟影響，特別是對原住民族與地方社區及其生計、食物系統、傳統農業實踐與生物文化豐富度等方面，進行研究與資訊交換之合作；</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"長期目標 A.10：使《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》締約方成為《名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與救濟補充議定書》之締約方，並建立履行該補充議定書下義務之措施","html":"<p>長期目標 A.10：使《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》締約方成為《名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與救濟補充議定書》之締約方，並建立履行該補充議定書下義務之措施</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"38. **鼓勵**《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》締約方視情況加入、批准、接受或核准《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之《名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與救濟補充議定書》；$^{22}$\n39. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，向締約方、原住民族與地方社區及相關利害關係人傳播關於該賠償責任與救濟補充議定書之資訊，並促進其推廣與意識提升，在可行時使用原住民族與地方社區之語言；","html":"<p>38. <strong>鼓勵</strong>《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》締約方視情況加入、批准、接受或核准《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之《名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與救濟補充議定書》；<sup>22</sup><br />\n39. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，向締約方、原住民族與地方社區及相關利害關係人傳播關於該賠償責任與救濟補充議定書之資訊，並促進其推廣與意識提升，在可行時使用原住民族與地方社區之語言；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"長期目標 B.1：締約方參與能力建構活動","html":"<p>長期目標 B.1：締約方參與能力建構活動</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"40. **呼籲**締約方與相關組織促進能力建構與發展，並考量國家所識別之需求與優先事項，以及第五次評估與審查《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》有效性之結果，以及執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估，針對能力需求仍最普遍之領域，即：\n(a) 風險評估、風險管理及其他科學與技術專業；\n(b) 採樣、檢測與鑑定；\n(c) 機構能力與人力資源；\n(d) 公眾意識、教育與參與；\n(e) 監測與報告；","html":"<p>40. <strong>呼籲</strong>締約方與相關組織促進能力建構與發展，並考量國家所識別之需求與優先事項，以及第五次評估與審查《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》有效性之結果，以及執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估，針對能力需求仍最普遍之領域，即：<br />\n(a) 風險評估、風險管理及其他科學與技術專業；<br />\n(b) 採樣、檢測與鑑定；<br />\n(c) 機構能力與人力資源；<br />\n(d) 公眾意識、教育與參與；<br />\n(e) 監測與報告；</p>","en":[5,6,7,8]},{"md":"41. **鼓勵**締約方相互合作以強化執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之能力，包括讓原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人參與，並重點關注開發中國家締約方之需求，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方；\n42. **邀請**技術與科學合作支援中心將生物安全納入其兩年一度的工作計畫，並作為生物安全能力建構與發展、資訊分享以及南北合作、南南合作與三角合作之樞紐；\n43. **呼籲**相關組織，並**邀請**技術與科學合作支援中心，協助締約方開發生物安全計畫提案；\n44. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：\n(a) 持續開展能力建構與發展活動，以協助締約方執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》，並定期提醒秘書處網站上提供之廣泛能力建構資料；$^{23}$","html":"<p>41. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方相互合作以強化執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之能力，包括讓原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人參與，並重點關注開發中國家締約方之需求，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方；<br />\n42. <strong>邀請</strong>技術與科學合作支援中心將生物安全納入其兩年一度的工作計畫，並作為生物安全能力建構與發展、資訊分享以及南北合作、南南合作與三角合作之樞紐；<br />\n43. <strong>呼籲</strong>相關組織，並<strong>邀請</strong>技術與科學合作支援中心，協助締約方開發生物安全計畫提案；<br />\n44. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：<br />\n(a) 持續開展能力建構與發展活動，以協助締約方執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》，並定期提醒秘書處網站上提供之廣泛能力建構資料；<sup>23</sup></p>","en":[9,10,11,12,13]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[14]},{"md":"$^{22}$ 決議 BS-V/11，附件。","html":"<p><sup>22</sup> 決議 BS-V/11，附件。</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"$^{23}$ https://bch.cbd.int/protocol.","html":"<p><sup>23</sup> https://bch.cbd.int/protocol.</p>","en":[15,16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p015","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p015.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"(b)    To facilitate capacity-building and development activities on designing biosafety projects;"},{"t":"(c) To raise awareness of funding mechanisms and processes for the submission of biosafety proposals;"},{"t":"Goal B.2: Parties mobilize adequate resources from all sources to support implementation of the Cartagena Protocol, in accordance with Article 28 of the Protocol"},{"t":"45. Urges Parties to allocate adequate resources to biosafety in their national budgets, in accordance with their national circumstances, priorities and capabilities;"},{"t":"46. Calls upon developed country Parties, in accordance with Article 28 of the Cartagena Protocol, and invites other Governments, international organizations, bilateral and multilateral funding agencies, regional development banks and other programmes and initiatives, to provide adequate, predictable and accessible financial resources and in-kind contributions, as appropriate, to support the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"Goal B.3: Parties promote and facilitate public awareness, education and participation on the safe transfer, handling and use of living modified organisms, in accordance with Article 23 of the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"47. Encourages Parties to consult the public in the decision-making process regarding living modified organisms and make the results of such decisions available to the public, while respecting confidential information, in accordance with Article 21 of the Cartagena Protocol and their respective laws and regulations, with a view to increasing transparency;"},{"t":"48. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to provide support for capacity-building and development on fulfilling the provisions of the Cartagena Protocol related to public awareness, education and participation concerning the safe transfer, handling and use of living modified organisms;"},{"t":"Goal B.4: Parties enhance cooperation and coordination on biosafety issues at the national, regional and international levels"},{"t":"49. Encourages Parties, as appropriate and in accordance with their national circumstances, priorities and existing institutional arrangements, to facilitate the integration of biosafety into cross-sectoral and sectoral legislation, regulations, policies, strategies, action plans, programmes and institutions;"},{"t":"50. Invites donor countries and relevant organizations to support Parties with the integration referred to in paragraph 49 above;"},{"t":"51. Encourages Parties to cooperate with the technical and scientific cooperation support centres and relevant organizations in the exchange of scientific, technical and institutional knowledge on biosafety, including at the regional and international levels[, while reaffirming that risk assessment and risk management are a matter of national determination, undertaken by Parties in accordance with the Cartagena Protocol and national legislation, priorities and circumstances, and encouraging transparency and scientific integrity, including through the identification, disclosure and appropriate management of conflict of interest in relevant processes];"},{"t":"52. Encourages Parties that have not yet done so to develop mechanisms for involving indigenous peoples and local communities in the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol."},{"t":"15/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"(b) 促進生物安全計畫設計之能力建構與發展活動；","html":"<p>(b) 促進生物安全計畫設計之能力建構與發展活動；</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"(c) 提高對於提交生物安全提案之資金機制與程序的認識；\n長期目標 B.2：締約方依據議定書第 28 條，從所有來源動員充足資源以支持卡塔赫納議定書之實施\n45. **敦促**締約方依據其國情、優先事項與能力，在其國家預算中為生物安全配置充足資源；\n46. **呼籲**已開發國家締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書第 28 條，並**邀請**其他政府、國際組織、雙邊與多邊資助機構、區域開發銀行及其他計畫與倡議，視情況提供充足、可預測且可取得的財務資源與實物捐助，以支持卡塔赫納議定書之實施；\n長期目標 B.3：締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書第 23 條，促進並便利大眾對於基因改造活生物體安全轉移、處理與使用之意識、教育與參與\n47. **鼓勵**締約方在有關基因改造活生物體的決策過程中諮詢大眾，並在尊重機密資訊之同時，依據卡塔赫納議定書第 21 條及其各自之法律與法規，將此類決策之結果提供給大眾，以期增加透明度；\n48. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織，針對履行卡塔赫納議定書中關於基因改造活生物體安全轉移、處理與使用之公眾意識、教育與參與之規定，提供能力建構與開發之支持；\n長期目標 B.4：締約方在國家、區域及國際層級上，加強生物安全議題之合作與協調\n49. **鼓勵**締約方視情況並依據其國情、優先事項與現有制度安排，促進將生物安全整合至跨部門與部門之立法、法規、政策、策略、行動計畫、計畫與制度中；\n50. **邀請**捐助國與相關組織，支持締約方進行上述第 49 段所述之整合；\n51. **鼓勵**締約方與技術及科學合作支援中心及相關組織合作，在區域與國際層級進行生物安全之科學、技術與制度知識交換，[, 並重申風險評估與風險管理乃屬國家自主事項，由締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書及國家立法、優先事項與情況所進行，並鼓勵透明度與科學誠信，包括透過在相關程序中識別、揭露及適當管理利益衝突]；\n52. **鼓勵**尚未採取行動之締約方，制定讓原住民族與地方社區參與卡塔赫納議定書實施之機制。","html":"<p>(c) 提高對於提交生物安全提案之資金機制與程序的認識；<br />\n長期目標 B.2：締約方依據議定書第 28 條，從所有來源動員充足資源以支持卡塔赫納議定書之實施<br />\n45. <strong>敦促</strong>締約方依據其國情、優先事項與能力，在其國家預算中為生物安全配置充足資源；<br />\n46. <strong>呼籲</strong>已開發國家締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書第 28 條，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、國際組織、雙邊與多邊資助機構、區域開發銀行及其他計畫與倡議，視情況提供充足、可預測且可取得的財務資源與實物捐助，以支持卡塔赫納議定書之實施；<br />\n長期目標 B.3：締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書第 23 條，促進並便利大眾對於基因改造活生物體安全轉移、處理與使用之意識、教育與參與<br />\n47. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方在有關基因改造活生物體的決策過程中諮詢大眾，並在尊重機密資訊之同時，依據卡塔赫納議定書第 21 條及其各自之法律與法規，將此類決策之結果提供給大眾，以期增加透明度；<br />\n48. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織，針對履行卡塔赫納議定書中關於基因改造活生物體安全轉移、處理與使用之公眾意識、教育與參與之規定，提供能力建構與開發之支持；<br />\n長期目標 B.4：締約方在國家、區域及國際層級上，加強生物安全議題之合作與協調<br />\n49. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方視情況並依據其國情、優先事項與現有制度安排，促進將生物安全整合至跨部門與部門之立法、法規、政策、策略、行動計畫、計畫與制度中；<br />\n50. <strong>邀請</strong>捐助國與相關組織，支持締約方進行上述第 49 段所述之整合；<br />\n51. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方與技術及科學合作支援中心及相關組織合作，在區域與國際層級進行生物安全之科學、技術與制度知識交換，[, 並重申風險評估與風險管理乃屬國家自主事項，由締約方依據卡塔赫納議定書及國家立法、優先事項與情況所進行，並鼓勵透明度與科學誠信，包括透過在相關程序中識別、揭露及適當管理利益衝突]；<br />\n52. <strong>鼓勵</strong>尚未採取行動之締約方，制定讓原住民族與地方社區參與卡塔赫納議定書實施之機制。</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]}]},{"p":"p016","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p016.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 9"},{"t":"Matters related to the financial mechanism and resources"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/7."},{"t":"Matters related to the financial mechanism and resources"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling Article 28 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,24"},{"t":"Having considered the information on biosafety in the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity,25,26"},{"t":"1.    Welcomes the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and its programming directions and the support thereby made available to Parties for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety, and expresses its appreciation to the countries that contributed to the replenishment;"},{"t":"2.     Welcomes with appreciation the measures taken by the Global Environment Facility to enhance the financial mechanism with respect to biosafety;"},{"t":"3.     Recommends that the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity give full consideration to the Cartagena Protocol in the terms of reference to be adopted for the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism under the Convention;"},{"t":"4.     Invites Parties to the Cartagena Protocol to contribute to and participate in the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism;"},{"t":"5.    Urges eligible Parties to use the resources allocated to biosafety activities by the Global Environment Facility through its System for Transparent Allocation of Resources and to integrate biosafety into their biodiversity projects, in accordance with nationally identified needs and priorities;"},{"t":"6.      Encourages eligible Parties:"},{"t":"(a) To include needs and provisions for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol in their national biodiversity finance plans;"},{"t":"(b) To cooperate at the regional and subregional levels, as appropriate, in order to prepare requests for support from the Global Environment Facility for joint projects contributing to the cost-effective sharing of resources, information, experiences and expertise and to maximize complementarities and opportunities in that regard;"},{"t":"(c) To contribute biosafety elements to the four-year outcome-oriented framework of programme priorities related to the use of Global Environment Facility resources for biodiversity for the period from July 2030 to June 2034;"},{"t":"24 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"25 Ibid., vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"26 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1."},{"t":"16/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 9\n與財務機制及資源相關事項\n以下決議草案轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/7。","html":"<p>項目 9<br />\n與財務機制及資源相關事項<br />\n以下決議草案轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/7。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"與財務機制及資源相關事項\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，","html":"<p>與財務機制及資源相關事項<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**回顧**《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 28 條，$^{24}$","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第 28 條，<sup>24</sup></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**考慮到**全球環境基金理事會為生物多樣性公約第十七屆締約方大會所提交報告中關於生物安全的資訊，$^{25,26}$","html":"<p><strong>考慮到</strong>全球環境基金理事會為生物多樣性公約第十七屆締約方大會所提交報告中關於生物安全的資訊，$^{25,26}$</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**全球環境基金信託基金的第九次增資及其計畫方向，以及藉此為締約方執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》所提供的支持，並對參與增資的國家表示感謝；\n2. **表示歡迎並感謝**全球環境基金為強化生物安全相關財務機制所採取的措施；\n3. **建議**生物多樣性公約締約方大會在採納關於公約下財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查的職權範圍時，應充分考慮《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》；\n4. **邀請**《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》締約方參與並為財務機制有效性的第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；\n5. **敦促**符合條件的締約方，應透過全球環境基金的資源透明分配系統，使用分配給生物安全活動的資源，並根據國家所識別的需求與優先事項，將生物安全納入其生物多樣性計畫中；\n6. **鼓勵**符合條件的締約方：","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金信託基金的第九次增資及其計畫方向，以及藉此為締約方執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》所提供的支持，並對參與增資的國家表示感謝；<br />\n2. <strong>表示歡迎並感謝</strong>全球環境基金為強化生物安全相關財務機制所採取的措施；<br />\n3. <strong>建議</strong>生物多樣性公約締約方大會在採納關於公約下財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查的職權範圍時，應充分考慮《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》；<br />\n4. <strong>邀請</strong>《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》締約方參與並為財務機制有效性的第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；<br />\n5. <strong>敦促</strong>符合條件的締約方，應透過全球環境基金的資源透明分配系統，使用分配給生物安全活動的資源，並根據國家所識別的需求與優先事項，將生物安全納入其生物多樣性計畫中；<br />\n6. <strong>鼓勵</strong>符合條件的締約方：</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"(a) 在其國家生物多樣性財務計畫中，納入執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》的需求與規定；\n(b) 在適當情況下，於區域及次區域層級進行合作，以準備向全球環境基金申請支持，用於共同計畫，藉此促進資源、資訊、經驗與專業知識之具成本效益的分享，並在此方面實現互補性與機會的最大化；\n(c) 為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間，關於使用全球環境基金生物多樣性資源之四年期、以成果為導向的計畫優先事項架構，貢獻生物安全要素；","html":"<p>(a) 在其國家生物多樣性財務計畫中，納入執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》的需求與規定；<br />\n(b) 在適當情況下，於區域及次區域層級進行合作，以準備向全球環境基金申請支持，用於共同計畫，藉此促進資源、資訊、經驗與專業知識之具成本效益的分享，並在此方面實現互補性與機會的最大化；<br />\n(c) 為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間，關於使用全球環境基金生物多樣性資源之四年期、以成果為導向的計畫優先事項架構，貢獻生物安全要素；</p>","en":[12,13,14,15]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[16]},{"md":"$^{24}$ United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.","html":"<p><sup>24</sup> United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"$^{25}$ 同上，vol. 1760, No. 30619.","html":"<p><sup>25</sup> 同上，vol. 1760, No. 30619.</p>","en":[17]},{"md":"$^{26}$ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.","html":"<p><sup>26</sup> CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.</p>","en":[18,19]}]},{"p":"p017","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p017.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"7.     Recommends that, in adopting its guidance to the Global Environment Facility with respect to support for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol, the Conference of the Parties to the Convention request the Facility:"},{"t":"(a) To make specific, adequate and timely funding available to eligible Parties for putting in place legal, administrative and other measures for implementing the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"(b)    To continue to provide support for the effective use of the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"(c) To assist eligible Parties by providing them, sufficiently in advance of the reporting deadline, with financial support to hold adequate national consultations, thus giving them enough time to prepare their sixth national reports and submit them in a timely manner;"},{"t":"(d) To make specific, adequate and timely funding available to eligible Parties to implement compliance action plans developed at the request of the Compliance Committee under the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"(e) To continue to support capacity-building and development on biosafety, [as part of country-driven projects,] including during the ninth replenishment period of its Trust Fund (July 2026−June 2030) and through the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, according to the mandates of the respective Funds[, and to establish [direct,] adequate, predictable and dedicated funding channels for biosafety to ensure that implementation needs are fully met];"},{"t":"8.    Requests the Executive Secretary to continue to explore other means for mobilizing additional financial resources for the implementation of the Cartagena Protocol and report on that work at the thirteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol."},{"t":"17/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"7. **建議**締約方大會於採納其向全球環境基金提供關於支持實施卡塔赫納議定書之指引時，請求該基金：\n(a) 向符合資格的締約方提供具體、充足且及時的資金，以建立實施卡塔赫納議定書之法律、行政及其他措施；\n(b) 持續為生物安全資訊交換所之有效利用提供支持；\n(c) 透過在報告截止日期前足夠的提前期提供財務支持，以協助符合資格的締約方進行充分的國家諮商，從而使該等締約方有足夠時間準備其第六次國家報告並及時提交；\n(d) 向符合資格的締約方提供具體、充足且及時的資金，以實施根據卡塔赫納議定書下遵約委員會請求所制定之遵約行動計畫；\n(e) 持續支持生物安全方面之能力建構與發展，[作為國家主導計畫的一部分，] 包括在其信託基金第九次增資期間（2026年7月－2030年6月）以及透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金（GBFF），根據各自基金之授權進行，[並為生物安全建立 [直接的]、充足、可預測且專用的資金管道，以確保實施需求得到充分滿足]；","html":"<p>7. <strong>建議</strong>締約方大會於採納其向全球環境基金提供關於支持實施卡塔赫納議定書之指引時，請求該基金：<br />\n(a) 向符合資格的締約方提供具體、充足且及時的資金，以建立實施卡塔赫納議定書之法律、行政及其他措施；<br />\n(b) 持續為生物安全資訊交換所之有效利用提供支持；<br />\n(c) 透過在報告截止日期前足夠的提前期提供財務支持，以協助符合資格的締約方進行充分的國家諮商，從而使該等締約方有足夠時間準備其第六次國家報告並及時提交；<br />\n(d) 向符合資格的締約方提供具體、充足且及時的資金，以實施根據卡塔赫納議定書下遵約委員會請求所制定之遵約行動計畫；<br />\n(e) 持續支持生物安全方面之能力建構與發展，[作為國家主導計畫的一部分，] 包括在其信託基金第九次增資期間（2026年7月－2030年6月）以及透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金（GBFF），根據各自基金之授權進行，[並為生物安全建立 [直接的]、充足、可預測且專用的資金管道，以確保實施需求得到充分滿足]；</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"8. **請求**執行秘書繼續探索其他動員額外財務資源之手段，以用於實施卡塔赫納議定書，並在第十三屆締約方大會（同時作為議定書締約方會議）時就該工作進行報告。","html":"<p>8. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書繼續探索其他動員額外財務資源之手段，以用於實施卡塔赫納議定書，並在第十三屆締約方大會（同時作為議定書締約方會議）時就該工作進行報告。</p>","en":[5,6,7,8]}]},{"p":"p018","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p018.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 10"},{"t":"Operation and activities of the Biosafety Clearing-House"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/8."},{"t":"Operation and activities of the Biosafety Clearing-House"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"1.     Welcomes with appreciation the work of the Informal Advisory Committee on the Biosafety Clearing-House, including the recommendations made at its thirteenth meeting27 and the support provided by the Committee for the development of the customized biosafety national website template using the Bioland tool;"},{"t":"2.    Welcomes progress towards Goal A.2 of the implementation plan for the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,28,29 in particular the increase in Parties publishing mandatory information through the Biosafety Clearing-House, and the ongoing efforts made by Parties to maintain accurate and complete information in the Clearing-House;"},{"t":"3.    Encourages Parties to continue to review their national records systematically, with a view to ensuring that the information made available through the Biosafety Clearing-House is up to date and complete;"},{"t":"4.     Reminds Parties of their obligation to publish the final decisions taken regarding the import or release of living modified organisms and corresponding summaries of risk assessments through the Biosafety Clearing-House, in compliance with Article 20 of the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"5.     Requests Parties to review the biosafety experts national records published through the Biosafety Clearing-House and associated with each Party, with a view to ensuring that the list of experts is up to date, outdated records are removed and all relevant experts are included;"},{"t":"6.     Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to make available and submit scientific information through the Biosafety Clearing-House, ensuring that sufficient technical detail is readily provided to support the timely review, validation and publication of records;"},{"t":"7.      Requests the Executive Secretary:"},{"t":"(a) To continue to maintain the Biosafety Clearing-House and to make any necessary improvements to it, including those recommended by the Informal Advisory Committee on the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"(b) To continue to update and publish reference records in the Biosafety Clearing-House and to support Parties in updating the biosafety experts national records referred to in paragraph 5 above;"},{"t":"(c) To make the new customized biosafety national website template available to all Parties wishing to develop a national biosafety website, support Parties using the Hermes national website tool in transitioning to the new template and provide capacity-building materials and training on the new template;"},{"t":"(d)     To continue to collaborate with other biosafety-related databases and organizations."},{"t":"27 CBD/CP/BCH-IAC/13/3/Rev.1, annex I."},{"t":"28 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"29 Decision 10/3, annex."},{"t":"18/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 10\n生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動\n以下決議草案係從文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/8 重製。","html":"<p>項目 10<br />\n生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動<br />\n以下決議草案係從文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/8 重製。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會","html":"<p>生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**並讚賞生物安全資訊交換所非正式諮詢委員會的工作，包括其第十三屆會議$^{27}$所提出的建議，以及該委員會為利用 Bioland 工具開發客製化國家生物安全網站範本所提供的支援；","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>並讚賞生物安全資訊交換所非正式諮詢委員會的工作，包括其第十三屆會議<sup>27</sup>所提出的建議，以及該委員會為利用 Bioland 工具開發客製化國家生物安全網站範本所提供的支援；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"2. **歡迎**卡塔赫納生物安全議定書執行計畫$^{28,29}$邁向長期目標 A.2 的進展，特別是透過生物安全資訊交換所公布強制性資訊的締約方有所增加，以及締約方為維持資訊交換所內資訊之準確性與完整性所持續進行的努力；","html":"<p>2. <strong>歡迎</strong>卡塔赫納生物安全議定書執行計畫$^{28,29}$邁向長期目標 A.2 的進展，特別是透過生物安全資訊交換所公布強制性資訊的締約方有所增加，以及締約方為維持資訊交換所內資訊之準確性與完整性所持續進行的努力；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"3. **鼓勵**締約方繼續系統性地審查其國家紀錄，以確保透過生物安全資訊交換所提供的資訊為最新且完整；","html":"<p>3. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方繼續系統性地審查其國家紀錄，以確保透過生物安全資訊交換所提供的資訊為最新且完整；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"4. **提醒**締約方，根據卡塔赫納議定書第 20 條，有義務透過生物安全資訊交換所公布關於基因改造活生物體進口或釋放之最終決定，以及相應的風險評估摘要；","html":"<p>4. <strong>提醒</strong>締約方，根據卡塔赫納議定書第 20 條，有義務透過生物安全資訊交換所公布關於基因改造活生物體進口或釋放之最終決定，以及相應的風險評估摘要；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"5. **請求**締約方審查透過生物安全資訊交換所公布且與各締約方相關之生物安全專家國家紀錄，以確保專家名單為最新狀態、移除過時紀錄，並納入所有相關專家；","html":"<p>5. <strong>請求</strong>締約方審查透過生物安全資訊交換所公布且與各締約方相關之生物安全專家國家紀錄，以確保專家名單為最新狀態、移除過時紀錄，並納入所有相關專家；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"6. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織透過生物安全資訊交換所提供並提交科學資訊，確保提供充足的技術細節，以支持紀錄的及時審查、驗證與公布；","html":"<p>6. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織透過生物安全資訊交換所提供並提交科學資訊，確保提供充足的技術細節，以支持紀錄的及時審查、驗證與公布；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"7. **請求**執行秘書：","html":"<p>7. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書：</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"(a) 繼續維護生物安全資訊交換所，並對其進行任何必要的改進，包括由生物安全資訊交換所非正式諮詢委員會所建議的改進；\n(b) 繼續更新並在生物安全資訊交換所公布參考紀錄，並支援締約方更新上述第 5 段所述之生物安全專家國家紀錄；\n(c) 向所有希望開發國家生物安全網站的締約方提供新的客製化國家生物安全網站範本，支援使用 Hermes 國家網站工具的締約方轉換至新範本，並針對新範本提供能力建構教材與培訓；\n(d) 繼續與其他生物安全相關資料庫及組織進行合作。","html":"<p>(a) 繼續維護生物安全資訊交換所，並對其進行任何必要的改進，包括由生物安全資訊交換所非正式諮詢委員會所建議的改進；<br />\n(b) 繼續更新並在生物安全資訊交換所公布參考紀錄，並支援締約方更新上述第 5 段所述之生物安全專家國家紀錄；<br />\n(c) 向所有希望開發國家生物安全網站的締約方提供新的客製化國家生物安全網站範本，支援使用 Hermes 國家網站工具的締約方轉換至新範本，並針對新範本提供能力建構教材與培訓；<br />\n(d) 繼續與其他生物安全相關資料庫及組織進行合作。</p>","en":[13,14,15]},{"md":"$^{27}$ CBD/CP/BCH-IAC/13/3/Rev.1, 附錄 I。\n$^{28}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{29}$ 決議 10/3, 附錄。","html":"<p><sup>27</sup> CBD/CP/BCH-IAC/13/3/Rev.1, 附錄 I。<br />\n<sup>28</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>29</sup> 決議 10/3, 附錄。</p>","en":[16,17,18,19,20]}]},{"p":"p019","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p019.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 11"},{"t":"Cooperation with international organizations,"},{"t":"bodies established under other conventions, and initiatives"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol is expected to take note of the information contained in document CBD/CP/MOP/12/9. No decision is expected under agenda item 11."},{"t":"19/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 11\n與國際組織、依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作\n作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，預期將注意到文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/9 中所含之資訊。議程第 11 項預期不採取任何決議。","html":"<p>項目 11<br />\n與國際組織、依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作<br />\n作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，預期將注意到文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/9 中所含之資訊。議程第 11 項預期不採取任何決議。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]}]},{"p":"p020","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p020.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 12"},{"t":"Review of the effectiveness of processes under"},{"t":"the Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols"},{"t":"The following draft decision comes from recommendation 6/8 of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation."},{"t":"Options for further improving the effectiveness of meetings under the Convention and its Protocols"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling its decision CP-11/5 of 1 November 2024,"},{"t":"Recognizing the need to ensure [the inclusiveness, transparency and equity][the integrity] of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety 30 while pursuing efficiencies and, where appropriate, the integration of processes with the Convention on Biological Diversity31 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization,32"},{"t":"Reaffirming the important role of technology in supporting the efficiency and effectiveness of meetings, without prejudice to decision-making by consensus,"},{"t":"1.    Takes note of decision 17/-- of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity;"},{"t":"2.     Welcomes the progress made with the decision-tracking tool developed further to decision XII/28 of 17 October 2014 of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention, as described in document CBD/SBI/6/INF/11;"},{"t":"3.     Decides that the decisions of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety should be included in the decision-tracking tool;"},{"t":"4.     Requests the Executive Secretary to take the necessary steps in that regard, beginning with decisions of its tenth and eleventh meetings;"},{"t":"5.    Recalls its decision BS-VII/9 of 3 October 2014, by which it decided to hold its ordinary meetings concurrently with the meetings of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention in the same two-week period in which the meetings of the Conference of the Parties of the Convention were held;"},{"t":"[6. Reiterates its call upon [developed country] Parties[, and other Parties in a position to do so,] [to increase their contributions][to contribute] to the relevant voluntary trust fund to ensure the full and effective participation of representatives of developing country Parties, in particular the least developed and small island developing States among them, and Parties with economies in transition in the concurrent meetings, and to increase their contribution to the Special Voluntary Trust Fund for Facilitating the Participation of Indigenous Peoples and Local Communities;]"},{"t":"7.    Notes that chairs of groups considering matters under the Cartagena Protocol are to be selected from among the Parties to the Protocol."},{"t":"30 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"31 Ibid., vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"32 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619."},{"t":"20/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 12\n審查《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下程序之成效\n下列決議草案源自執行附屬機構之建議 6/8。","html":"<p>項目 12<br />\n審查《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下程序之成效<br />\n下列決議草案源自執行附屬機構之建議 6/8。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"進一步提升《公約》及其議定書下會議成效之選項\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，","html":"<p>進一步提升《公約》及其議定書下會議成效之選項<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 CP-11/5，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 CP-11/5，</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"**認識到**在追求效率以及在適當時整合與《生物多樣性公約》$^{31}$及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其成果之名古屋議定書》$^{32}$之程序時，有必要確保卡塔赫納生物安全議定書$^{30}$之[包容性、透明度與公平性][完整性]；","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>在追求效率以及在適當時整合與《生物多樣性公約》<sup>31</sup>及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其成果之名古屋議定書》<sup>32</sup>之程序時，有必要確保卡塔赫納生物安全議定書<sup>30</sup>之[包容性、透明度與公平性][完整性]；</p>","en":[7,8]},{"md":"**重申**技術在支持會議效率與成效方面扮演重要角色，且不損及以共識進行決策；","html":"<p><strong>重申</strong>技術在支持會議效率與成效方面扮演重要角色，且不損及以共識進行決策；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"1. **注意到**生物多樣性公約締約方大會之決議 17/--；\n2. **歡迎**如文件 CBD/SBI/6/INF/11 所述，根據締約方大會 2014 年 10 月 17 日決議 XII/28 進一步開發之決議追蹤工具所取得之進展；\n3. **決定**擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會之決議，應納入決議追蹤工具中；\n4. **請求**執行秘書就此採取必要步驟，並從其第十及第十一屆會議之決議開始；\n5. **回顧**其 2014 年 10 月 3 日之決議 BS-VII/9，該決議決定其定期會議應與締約方大會會議於同一兩週期間內同時舉行；\n[6. 重申其呼籲：[已開發國家]締約方[, 以及其他有能力之締約方,] [應增加其捐款][應捐款]至相關自願信託基金，以確保開發中國家締約方代表（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方在同時舉行的會議中能充分且有效地參與，並增加其對促進原住民族與地方社區參與特別自願信託基金之捐款；]\n7. **注意到**審議卡塔赫納議定書下事項之小組主席，應從議定書締約方中選出。","html":"<p>1. <strong>注意到</strong>生物多樣性公約締約方大會之決議 17/--；<br />\n2. <strong>歡迎</strong>如文件 CBD/SBI/6/INF/11 所述，根據締約方大會 2014 年 10 月 17 日決議 XII/28 進一步開發之決議追蹤工具所取得之進展；<br />\n3. <strong>決定</strong>擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會之決議，應納入決議追蹤工具中；<br />\n4. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書就此採取必要步驟，並從其第十及第十一屆會議之決議開始；<br />\n5. <strong>回顧</strong>其 2014 年 10 月 3 日之決議 BS-VII/9，該決議決定其定期會議應與締約方大會會議於同一兩週期間內同時舉行；<br />\n[6. 重申其呼籲：[已開發國家]締約方[, 以及其他有能力之締約方,] [應增加其捐款][應捐款]至相關自願信託基金，以確保開發中國家締約方代表（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方在同時舉行的會議中能充分且有效地參與，並增加其對促進原住民族與地方社區參與特別自願信託基金之捐款；]<br />\n7. <strong>注意到</strong>審議卡塔赫納議定書下事項之小組主席，應從議定書締約方中選出。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"$^{30}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{31}$ 同上，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{32}$ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p><sup>30</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>31</sup> 同上，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>32</sup> 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[15,16,17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p021","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p021.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 13"},{"t":"Risk assessment and risk management of living modified organisms"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from recommendation 27/7 of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice."},{"t":"Risk assessment and risk management of living modified organisms"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling its decisions CP-9/13 of 28 November 2018 and CP-11/7 of 30 October 2024,"},{"t":"1.    Expresses appreciation for the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment33 and its application of the criteria set out in annex I to decision CP-9/13 to the topics proposed by Parties in relation to needs and priorities for further guidance on specific topics of risk assessment of living modified organisms;34"},{"t":"[2. Decides to develop a maximum of two additional voluntary guidance materials in accordance with annex III to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,35 for the topics of [living modified algae,] [living modified fish,] [living modified microorganisms,] [living modified organisms expressing genome editing machinery for pest or pathogen control,] [long-term and cumulative effects of genetic constructs and living modified organisms,] [operationalizing protection goals into relevant assessment and measurement end points,] [the use of living modified organisms in centres of origin and in traditional agricultural systems], while avoiding duplication with and, where appropriate, supplementing existing guidance materials;]"},{"t":"[3. Also decides to expand capacity-building efforts on the risk assessment and risk management of living modified organisms, making use of existing information, approaches and guidance materials on the topic, including those produced under the Cartagena Protocol, such as Biosafety Technical Series 07;]"},{"t":"[3.alt Also decides to expand capacity-building efforts on the risk assessment and risk management of living modified organisms, making use of existing information, guidance materials and the approach to risk assessment of living modified organisms described in Biosafety Technical Series 07;]"},{"t":"[4. Further decides to establish a new ad hoc technical expert group on risk assessment, with the terms of reference contained in the annex to the present decision;]"},{"t":"[5. Invites Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth, academia and relevant organizations to submit relevant information, such as national and regional risk assessment experiences and existing resources for risk assessment for the selected topics, to support the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment;]"},{"t":"[6. Decides to extend the Open-ended Online Forum on Risk Assessment and Risk Management to support the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment;]"},{"t":"[7. Also decides to consider at its thirteenth meeting additional issues on which guidance materials on risk assessment may be needed, further to the process established in decision CP-9/13 for the identification and prioritization of specific issues of risk assessment of living modified organisms that may warrant consideration, taking into account the priorities identified by Parties,"},{"t":"33 See CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/3."},{"t":"34 See CBD/SBSTTA/27/6, annex."},{"t":"35 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"21/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 13\n基因改造活生物體的風險評估與風險管理\n以下決議草案轉載自科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構之建議 27/7。","html":"<p>項目 13<br />\n基因改造活生物體的風險評估與風險管理<br />\n以下決議草案轉載自科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構之建議 27/7。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"基因改造活生物體的風險評估與風險管理\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，","html":"<p>基因改造活生物體的風險評估與風險管理<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會，</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2018 年 11 月 28 日之決議 CP-9/13 及 2024 年 10 月 30 日之決議 CP-11/7，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2018 年 11 月 28 日之決議 CP-9/13 及 2024 年 10 月 30 日之決議 CP-11/7，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"1. **表示**對風險評估特設技術專家小組$^{33}$的工作及其將決議 CP-9/13 附件 I 所列之標準，應用於締約方針對基因改造活生物體風險評估特定主題進一步指引之需求與優先事項所提出主題之工作，表示讚賞；$^{34}$","html":"<p>1. <strong>表示</strong>對風險評估特設技術專家小組<sup>33</sup>的工作及其將決議 CP-9/13 附件 I 所列之標準，應用於締約方針對基因改造活生物體風險評估特定主題進一步指引之需求與優先事項所提出主題之工作，表示讚賞；<sup>34</sup></p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[2. **決定**根據卡塔赫納生物安全議定書附件 III$^{35}$，針對[基因改造藻類、][基因改造魚類、][基因改造微生物、][表達用於害蟲或病原體控制之基因編輯機制的基因改造活生物體、][基因構築體與基因改造活生物體之長期與累積效應、][將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點、][基因改造活生物體在起源中心及傳統農業系統中的使用]等主題，開發最多兩份額外的自願性指引材料，同時避免與現有指引材料重複，並在適當時予以補充；]","html":"<p>[2. <strong>決定</strong>根據卡塔赫納生物安全議定書附件 III<sup>35</sup>，針對[基因改造藻類、][基因改造魚類、][基因改造微生物、][表達用於害蟲或病原體控制之基因編輯機制的基因改造活生物體、][基因構築體與基因改造活生物體之長期與累積效應、][將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點、][基因改造活生物體在起源中心及傳統農業系統中的使用]等主題，開發最多兩份額外的自願性指引材料，同時避免與現有指引材料重複，並在適當時予以補充；]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"[3. **亦決定**擴大基因改造活生物體風險評估與風險管理之能力建構工作，利用該主題現有的資訊、方法與指引材料，包括在卡塔赫納生物安全議定書下產生的材料，例如生物安全技術系列 07；]","html":"<p>[3. <strong>亦決定</strong>擴大基因改造活生物體風險評估與風險管理之能力建構工作，利用該主題現有的資訊、方法與指引材料，包括在卡塔赫納生物安全議定書下產生的材料，例如生物安全技術系列 07；]</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[3.alt **亦決定**擴大基因改造活生物體風險評估與風險管理之能力建構工作，利用現有的資訊、指引材料以及在生物安全技術系列 07 中所述之基因改造活生物體風險評估方法；]","html":"<p>[3.alt <strong>亦決定</strong>擴大基因改造活生物體風險評估與風險管理之能力建構工作，利用現有的資訊、指引材料以及在生物安全技術系列 07 中所述之基因改造活生物體風險評估方法；]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"[4. **進一步決定**成立一個新的風險評估特設技術專家小組，其職權範圍包含在本決議之附件中；]","html":"<p>[4. <strong>進一步決定</strong>成立一個新的風險評估特設技術專家小組，其職權範圍包含在本決議之附件中；]</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"[5. **邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、學術界及相關組織，提交相關資訊，例如國家與區域風險評估經驗以及針對所選主題之現有風險評估資源，以支持風險評估特設技術專家小組之工作；]","html":"<p>[5. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、學術界及相關組織，提交相關資訊，例如國家與區域風險評估經驗以及針對所選主題之現有風險評估資源，以支持風險評估特設技術專家小組之工作；]</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"[6. **決定**將風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇予以延伸，以支持風險評估特設技術專家小組之工作；]","html":"<p>[6. <strong>決定</strong>將風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇予以延伸，以支持風險評估特設技術專家小組之工作；]</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"[7. **亦決定**在其第十三屆會議上，考慮除了決議 CP-9/13 所建立之程序（用於識別與優先排序可能需要考慮之基因改造活生物體風險評估特定議題）之外，可能需要風險評估指引材料之額外議題，並考慮締約方所確定之優先事項，","html":"<p>[7. <strong>亦決定</strong>在其第十三屆會議上，考慮除了決議 CP-9/13 所建立之程序（用於識別與優先排序可能需要考慮之基因改造活生物體風險評估特定議題）之外，可能需要風險評估指引材料之額外議題，並考慮締約方所確定之優先事項，</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"$^{33}$ 參見 CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/3。\n$^{34}$ 參見 CBD/SBSTTA/27/6，附件。\n$^{35}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p><sup>33</sup> 參見 CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/3。<br />\n<sup>34</sup> 參見 CBD/SBSTTA/27/6，附件。<br />\n<sup>35</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[14,15,16,17]}]},{"p":"p022","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p022.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"including in their national reports, and the topics identified by the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment;36]"},{"t":"[8. Invites Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and women, youth and relevant organizations to submit information on experiences with the implementation of the simplified procedure provided in Article 13 of the Cartagena Protocol, bilateral, regional and multilateral agreements and arrangements provided in Article 14 of the Protocol, and on the transportability of data for risk assessment of living modified organisms[, recognizing that the acceptance of risk assessment data from other countries shall be subject to national evaluation and confirmation of ecological relevance and comparability];]"},{"t":"[9. Decides to consider at its thirteenth meeting the information submitted in response to paragraph 8 above;]"},{"t":"10. Urges Parties, and invites other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and women, youth and relevant organizations, to engage in broad international cooperation to share information and experiences related to risk assessment, in particular through the Biosafety Clearing-House, and promote capacity-building and development activities with regard to the topics prioritized by the [Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment;37][Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice;]"},{"t":"11. Invites the regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres 38 to assist Parties in addressing their needs and priorities on risk assessment and risk management;"},{"t":"12.     Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of financial resources: [(a) To convene at least two meetings of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment, one of which will be in person, before the thirteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol;]"},{"t":"[(b) To convene discussions in the Open-ended Online Forum on Risk Assessment and Risk Management during the same intersessional period and encourage the active participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth organizations, academia and other relevant organizations;]"},{"t":"(c) To synthesize information collected in response to paragraphs [5] and [8] of the present decision[ and through the Open-ended Online Forum on Risk Assessment and Risk Management], as well as the information related to specific needs for further guidance on specific topics of risk assessment and risk management in national reports;39"},{"t":"(d) To continue to undertake capacity-building and development activities on existing guidance materials through regional workshops in order to support the risk assessment of living modified organisms, in collaboration with relevant initiatives and partnerships, as appropriate, ensuring equitable representation of all developing country Parties;"},{"t":"(e) To continue to collect experiences on and assessments of the applicability and usefulness of the additional voluntary guidance materials to support case-by-case risk assessments of living modified organisms containing engineered gene drives40 and make them available through the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"36 [Living modified algae,] [living modified fish,] [living modified microorganisms,] [living modified organisms expressing"},{"t":"genome editing machinery for pest or pathogen control,] [long-term and cumulative effects of genetic constructs and living modified organisms,] [operationalizing protection goals into relevant assessment and measurement end points,] [the use of living modified organisms in centres of origin and in traditional agricultural systems]."},{"t":"37 See CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/3."},{"t":"38 See www.cbd.int/tsc/tscm/subregionalcentres."},{"t":"39 As provided in response to question 68 of the fifth national report under the Cartagena Protocol."},{"t":"40 See CBD/CP/MOP/11/9."},{"t":"22/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"包括其國家報告中，以及由風險評估特設技術專家小組所識別之主題；$^{36}$]\n[8. **邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性、青年與相關組織，提交關於執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第13條所規定之簡化程序、議定書第14條所規定之雙邊、區域及多邊協議與安排之經驗資訊，以及關於基因改造活生物體風險評估資料之可傳輸性資訊[, 並承認接受來自其他國家之風險評估資料應取決於國家對生態相關性與可比性的評估與確認];]\n[9. **決定**在其第十三屆會議審議針對上述第8段所提交之資訊；]\n10. **敦促**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性、青年與相關組織，參與廣泛的國際合作，以分享與風險評估相關之資訊與經驗，特別是透過生物安全資訊交換所，並針對[風險評估特設技術專家小組；$^{37}$][科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構；]所優先考慮之主題，促進能力建構與發展活動；\n11. **邀請**區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心 $^{38}$，協助締約方應對其在風險評估與風險管理方面之需求與優先事項；\n12. **請求**執行秘書，在財務資源可用之情況下：","html":"<p>包括其國家報告中，以及由風險評估特設技術專家小組所識別之主題；<sup>36</sup>]<br />\n[8. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性、青年與相關組織，提交關於執行《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第13條所規定之簡化程序、議定書第14條所規定之雙邊、區域及多邊協議與安排之經驗資訊，以及關於基因改造活生物體風險評估資料之可傳輸性資訊[, 並承認接受來自其他國家之風險評估資料應取決於國家對生態相關性與可比性的評估與確認];]<br />\n[9. <strong>決定</strong>在其第十三屆會議審議針對上述第8段所提交之資訊；]<br />\n10. <strong>敦促</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性、青年與相關組織，參與廣泛的國際合作，以分享與風險評估相關之資訊與經驗，特別是透過生物安全資訊交換所，並針對[風險評估特設技術專家小組；<sup>37</sup>][科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構；]所優先考慮之主題，促進能力建構與發展活動；<br />\n11. <strong>邀請</strong>區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心 <sup>38</sup>，協助締約方應對其在風險評估與風險管理方面之需求與優先事項；<br />\n12. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書，在財務資源可用之情況下：</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"[(a) 在擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第十三屆會議之前，至少召開兩次風險評估特設技術專家小組會議，其中一次應為實體會議；]\n[(b) 在同一會期內，於風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇召開討論，並鼓勵原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、學術界及其他相關組織之積極參與；]\n(c) 綜合收集針對本決議第[5]及第[8]段所作回應之資訊[以及透過風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇所獲取之資訊]，以及國家報告中與風險評估及風險管理特定主題進一步指引之特定需求相關之資訊；$^{39}$\n(d) 透過區域工作坊，針對現有指引材料持續開展能力建構與發展活動，以支持基因改造活生物體之風險評估，並視需要與相關倡議及夥伴關係合作，確保所有開發中國家締約方皆能獲得公平代表；\n(e) 持續收集關於額外自願性指引材料之適用性與有用性之經驗與評估，以支持含有工程基因驅動之基因改造活生物體之個案風險評估 $^{40}$，並透過生物安全資訊交換所提供該等資訊；","html":"<p>[(a) 在擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第十三屆會議之前，至少召開兩次風險評估特設技術專家小組會議，其中一次應為實體會議；]<br />\n[(b) 在同一會期內，於風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇召開討論，並鼓勵原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、學術界及其他相關組織之積極參與；]<br />\n(c) 綜合收集針對本決議第[5]及第[8]段所作回應之資訊[以及透過風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇所獲取之資訊]，以及國家報告中與風險評估及風險管理特定主題進一步指引之特定需求相關之資訊；<sup>39</sup><br />\n(d) 透過區域工作坊，針對現有指引材料持續開展能力建構與發展活動，以支持基因改造活生物體之風險評估，並視需要與相關倡議及夥伴關係合作，確保所有開發中國家締約方皆能獲得公平代表；<br />\n(e) 持續收集關於額外自願性指引材料之適用性與有用性之經驗與評估，以支持含有工程基因驅動之基因改造活生物體之個案風險評估 <sup>40</sup>，並透過生物安全資訊交換所提供該等資訊；</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"$^{36}$ [基因改造藻類,] [基因改造魚類,] [基因改造微生物,] [表達用於害蟲或病原體控制之基因編輯機制的基因改造活生物體,] [基因構築體與基因改造活生物體之長期與累積效應,] [將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點,] [基因改造活生物體在起源中心及傳統農業系統中之使用]。\n$^{37}$ 見 CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/3。\n$^{38}$ 見 www.cbd.int/tsc/tscm/subregionalcentres。\n$^{39}$ 如《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第五份國家報告中針對第68題之回應所提供。\n$^{40}$ 見 CBD/CP/MOP/11/9。","html":"<p><sup>36</sup> [基因改造藻類,] [基因改造魚類,] [基因改造微生物,] [表達用於害蟲或病原體控制之基因編輯機制的基因改造活生物體,] [基因構築體與基因改造活生物體之長期與累積效應,] [將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點,] [基因改造活生物體在起源中心及傳統農業系統中之使用]。<br />\n<sup>37</sup> 見 CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/3。<br />\n<sup>38</sup> 見 www.cbd.int/tsc/tscm/subregionalcentres。<br />\n<sup>39</sup> 如《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第五份國家報告中針對第68題之回應所提供。<br />\n<sup>40</sup> 見 CBD/CP/MOP/11/9。</p>","en":[11,12,13,14,15]}]},{"p":"p023","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p023.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"[13. Requests the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice to consider the outcomes of the meetings of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment at a meeting held before the thirteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol and to make recommendations to the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol for consideration at its thirteenth meeting.]"},{"t":"["},{"t":"Annex"},{"t":"Terms of reference for the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment"},{"t":"1.      The Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Risk Assessment shall:"},{"t":"(a) Be composed of experts, selected in accordance with section H of the consolidated modus operandi of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice,41 with specific scientific and technical expertise relevant to the present mandate, and include experts from academia, relevant international organizations and indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, in line with decision 14/33 of 29 November 2018 on the procedure for avoiding or managing conflicts of interest in expert groups, as amended in decision CP-11/6 of 1 November 2024;"},{"t":"(b) Subject to the availability of funds, hold at least two meetings, one of which will be in person, before the thirteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety42 and perform any necessary tasks between its two meetings by online means of communication and engagement;"},{"t":"(c) Develop draft additional voluntary guidance materials for living modified microorganisms and living modified fish, in accordance with annex III to the Cartagena Protocol, taking into account approaches to risk assessment set out in the additional voluntary guidance materials to support case-by-case risk assessments of living modified organisms containing engineered gene drives43 and avoiding duplication with existing guidance materials, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body at a meeting held before the thirteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol;"},{"t":"(d) [Develop draft technical notes 44 for voluntary use for the topics of operationalizing protection goals into relevant assessment and measurement end points and the use of living modified organisms in centres of origin and in traditional agricultural systems], 45 [Develop concise supplementary guidance for voluntary use that provides specific, clear and focused information on [living modified algae,] [living modified fish,] [living modified microorganisms,] [living modified organisms expressing genome editing machinery for pest or pathogen control,] [long-term and cumulative effects of genetic constructs and living modified organisms,] [operationalizing protection goals into relevant assessment and measurement end points,] [the use of living modified organisms in centres of origin and in traditional agricultural systems]] in accordance with annex III to the Cartagena Protocol and avoiding duplication with existing guidance materials, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body at a meeting held before the thirteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties"},{"t":"41 Decision VIII/10, annex III."},{"t":"42 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"43 See CBD/CP/MOP/11/9."},{"t":"44 A technical note may be a concise document that provides practical information on a specific topic or issue. It supplements"},{"t":"existing guidance materials and may include procedural elements or points to consider when addressing a specific topic or context."},{"t":"45 The technical note on the use of living modified organisms in centres of origin and in traditional agricultural systems should be"},{"t":"consistent with the Akwé: Kon Voluntary Guidelines for the Conduct of Cultural, Environmental and Social Impact Assessments regarding Developments Proposed to Take Place on, or which are Likely to Impact On, Sacred Sites and On Lands and Waters Traditionally Occupied or Used by Indigenous and Local Communities."},{"t":"23/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"[13. **請求**科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構在擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的第十三屆締約方大會召開前，審議風險評估特設技術專家小組會議之成果，並向擔任該議定書締約方會議的締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十三屆會議審議。]","html":"<p>[13. <strong>請求</strong>科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構在擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的第十三屆締約方大會召開前，審議風險評估特設技術專家小組會議之成果，並向擔任該議定書締約方會議的締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十三屆會議審議。]</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"[\n附錄\n風險評估特設技術專家小組職權範圍\n1.","html":"<p>[<br />\n附錄<br />\n風險評估特設技術專家小組職權範圍<br />\n1.</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"風險評估特設技術專家小組應：","html":"<p>風險評估特設技術專家小組應：</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(a) 根據科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構綜合作業程序第 H 節，$^{41}$ 選任具備與本授權相關之特定科學與技術專業知識之專家組成，並根據 2018 年 11 月 29 日關於專家小組避免或管理利益衝突程序之決議 14/33（經 2024 年 11 月 1 日決議 CP-11/6 修訂），納入來自學術界、相關國際組織、原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的專家；\n(b) 在撥款可用的情況下，於擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的第十三屆締約方大會 $^{42}$ 前，至少召開兩次會議（其中一次應為實體會議），並透過線上溝通與參與方式，在其兩次會議之間執行任何必要任務；\n(c) 根據卡塔赫納議定書附件 III，針對基因改造微生物與基因改造魚類，制定自願性額外指引材料草案，並考量用於支持含有工程基因驅動之基因改造活生物體 $^{43}$ 個案風險評估之風險評估方法，且應避免與現有指引材料重複，以供附屬機構在擔任該議定書締約方會議的第十三屆締約方大會召開前之會議審議；\n(d) [針對將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點的操作化，以及在起源中心與傳統農業系統中使用基因改造活生物體之主題，制定供自願使用的技術說明草案 $^{44}$]，$^{45}$ [根據卡塔赫納議定書附件 III，制定供自願使用的簡明補充指導，針對 [基因改造藻類]、[基因改造魚類]、[基因改造微生物]、[表達用於害蟲或病原體控制之基因編輯機制的基因改造活生物體]、[基因構築體與基因改造活生物體的長期與累積效應]、[將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點的操作化]、[在起源中心與傳統農業系統中使用基因改造活生物體] 提供具體、清晰且聚焦之資訊，並避免與現有指引材料重複，以供附屬機構在第十三屆締約方大會召開前之會議審議]]","html":"<p>(a) 根據科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構綜合作業程序第 H 節，<sup>41</sup> 選任具備與本授權相關之特定科學與技術專業知識之專家組成，並根據 2018 年 11 月 29 日關於專家小組避免或管理利益衝突程序之決議 14/33（經 2024 年 11 月 1 日決議 CP-11/6 修訂），納入來自學術界、相關國際組織、原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的專家；<br />\n(b) 在撥款可用的情況下，於擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的第十三屆締約方大會 <sup>42</sup> 前，至少召開兩次會議（其中一次應為實體會議），並透過線上溝通與參與方式，在其兩次會議之間執行任何必要任務；<br />\n(c) 根據卡塔赫納議定書附件 III，針對基因改造微生物與基因改造魚類，制定自願性額外指引材料草案，並考量用於支持含有工程基因驅動之基因改造活生物體 <sup>43</sup> 個案風險評估之風險評估方法，且應避免與現有指引材料重複，以供附屬機構在擔任該議定書締約方會議的第十三屆締約方大會召開前之會議審議；<br />\n(d) [針對將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點的操作化，以及在起源中心與傳統農業系統中使用基因改造活生物體之主題，制定供自願使用的技術說明草案 <sup>44</sup>]，<sup>45</sup> [根據卡塔赫納議定書附件 III，制定供自願使用的簡明補充指導，針對 [基因改造藻類]、[基因改造魚類]、[基因改造微生物]、[表達用於害蟲或病原體控制之基因編輯機制的基因改造活生物體]、[基因構築體與基因改造活生物體的長期與累積效應]、[將保護目標轉化為相關評估與衡量終點的操作化]、[在起源中心與傳統農業系統中使用基因改造活生物體] 提供具體、清晰且聚焦之資訊，並避免與現有指引材料重複，以供附屬機構在第十三屆締約方大會召開前之會議審議]]</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"$^{41}$ 決議 VIII/10，附件 III。\n$^{42}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{43}$ 參見 CBD/CP/MOP/11/9。\n$^{44}$ 技術說明可為一份簡明文件，提供關於特定主題或議題的實務資訊。其補充了現有的指引材料，並可能包含處理特定主題或情境時的程序性要素或應考慮之要點。\n$^{45}$ 關於在起源中心與傳統農業系統中使用基因改造活生物體的技術說明，應與《針對擬在原住民族與地方社區傳統佔用或使用的聖地、土地與水域進行開發或可能產生影響之開發案，進行文化、環境與社會影響評估之 Akwé: Kon 自願性指南》保持一致。","html":"<p><sup>41</sup> 決議 VIII/10，附件 III。<br />\n<sup>42</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>43</sup> 參見 CBD/CP/MOP/11/9。<br />\n<sup>44</sup> 技術說明可為一份簡明文件，提供關於特定主題或議題的實務資訊。其補充了現有的指引材料，並可能包含處理特定主題或情境時的程序性要素或應考慮之要點。<br />\n<sup>45</sup> 關於在起源中心與傳統農業系統中使用基因改造活生物體的技術說明，應與《針對擬在原住民族與地方社區傳統佔用或使用的聖地、土地與水域進行開發或可能產生影響之開發案，進行文化、環境與社會影響評估之 Akwé: Kon 自願性指南》保持一致。</p>","en":[12,13,14,15,16]}]},{"p":"p024","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p024.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol. [The guidance may include procedural or practical elements or points to consider during risk assessment.]"},{"t":"2.    In conducting its work, the Expert Group shall consider the information submitted pursuant to paragraph 5 of the present decision, the discussions held in the Open-ended Online Forum on Risk Assessment and Risk Management, the synthesis of information prepared by the Secretariat pursuant to paragraph 12 (c) of the present decision, the synthesis of submissions of information on risk assessment and the discussions held in the Online Forum 46 and the list of bibliographical references provided in the submissions from Parties and during the discussions held in the Online Forum.47"},{"t":"3.     In conducting its work, the Expert Group shall also consider information produced by other international, regional and national bodies, to avoid the duplication of existing materials. ]"},{"t":"46 CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/INF/1."},{"t":"47 CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/INF/2."},{"t":"24/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"作為議定書締約方會議。[指引可能包括程序性或實務性要素，或在風險評估期間應考慮的要點。]\n2. 在進行其工作時，專家小組應考慮根據本決議第 5 段所提交的資訊、在風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇中進行的討論、秘書處根據本決議第 12 (c) 段所編製的資訊綜合報告、關於風險評估之資訊提交的綜合報告以及在線上論壇中進行的討論$^{46}$，以及締約方在提交資料時及線上論壇討論期間所提供的參考文獻清單$^{47}$。\n3. 在進行其工作時，專家小組亦應考慮由其他國際、區域及國家機構所產生的資訊，以避免與現有資料重複。\n]","html":"<p>作為議定書締約方會議。[指引可能包括程序性或實務性要素，或在風險評估期間應考慮的要點。]<br />\n2. 在進行其工作時，專家小組應考慮根據本決議第 5 段所提交的資訊、在風險評估與風險管理開放式線上論壇中進行的討論、秘書處根據本決議第 12 (c) 段所編製的資訊綜合報告、關於風險評估之資訊提交的綜合報告以及在線上論壇中進行的討論<sup>46</sup>，以及締約方在提交資料時及線上論壇討論期間所提供的參考文獻清單<sup>47</sup>。<br />\n3. 在進行其工作時，專家小組亦應考慮由其他國際、區域及國家機構所產生的資訊，以避免與現有資料重複。<br />\n]</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"$^{46}$ CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/INF/1.\n$^{47}$ CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/INF/2.","html":"<p><sup>46</sup> CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/INF/1.<br />\n<sup>47</sup> CBD/CP/RA/AHTEG/2025/1/INF/2.</p>","en":[3,4,5,6]}]},{"p":"p025","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p025.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 14"},{"t":"Detection and identification of living modified organisms"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/10."},{"t":"Detection and identification of living modified organisms"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol, Recalling its decisions CP-10/11 of 10 December 2022 and CP-11/8 of 30 October 2024, Noting the progress reported by Parties in their fifth national reports in relation to the detection and identification of living modified organisms under the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,48 and acknowledging the findings of the fifth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Protocol,49"},{"t":"Noting also the challenges faced by many Parties in ensuring the sustainable operation, maintenance and continuous development of laboratory facilities involved in the detection and identification of living modified organisms and the significant differences in technical and institutional capacities that continue to exist among Parties,"},{"t":"1.     Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to review and update, as appropriate, the information contained in the registry of laboratories available through the Biosafety Clearing-House and to nominate additional laboratories and experts to participate in the Network of Laboratories for the Detection and Identification of Living Modified Organisms;"},{"t":"2.     Encourages Parties to support the establishment, revitalization and strengthening of regional networks of laboratories and partnerships to promote capacity-building, knowledge-sharing and technical cooperation in the detection and identification of living modified organisms;"},{"t":"3.     Also encourages Parties to develop long-term national strategies for the sustainable operation, maintenance and continuous development of laboratory facilities involved in the detection and identification of living modified organisms, including through institutional support and regional cooperation;"},{"t":"4.     Invites Parties, other Governments and international organizations to provide financial resources, in particular for developing countries, especially the least developed countries and small island developing States, and countries with economies in transition to strengthen laboratory infrastructure, technical expertise and laboratory quality control systems for the detection and identification of living modified organisms;"},{"t":"5.    Decides to develop a supplemental chapter on digital polymerase chain reaction to complement the Training Manual on the Detection and Identification of Living Modified Organisms in the Context of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety (Biosafety Technical Series No. 5);"},{"t":"6.      Requests the Executive Secretary:"},{"t":"(a) To draft the supplemental chapter on digital polymerase chain reaction referred to in paragraph 5 above, in collaboration with the Network of Laboratories for the Detection and Identification of Living Modified Organisms;"},{"t":"(b) To convene online discussions of the Network of Laboratories to facilitate the development and peer review of the supplemental chapter, for its subsequent consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice;"},{"t":"48 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"49 See CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1."},{"t":"25/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 14\n基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定\n以下決議草案係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/10。","html":"<p>項目 14<br />\n基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定<br />\n以下決議草案係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/10。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，","html":"<p>基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2022 年 12 月 10 日之決議 CP-10/11 及 2024 年 10 月 30 日之決議 CP-11/8，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2022 年 12 月 10 日之決議 CP-10/11 及 2024 年 10 月 30 日之決議 CP-11/8，</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**注意到**締約方在其第五份國家報告中，針對卡塔赫納生物安全議定書下基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定所報告之進展，$^{48}$ 並**承認**對議定書有效性進行第五次評估與審查之結果，$^{49}$","html":"<p><strong>注意到</strong>締約方在其第五份國家報告中，針對卡塔赫納生物安全議定書下基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定所報告之進展，<sup>48</sup> 並<strong>承認</strong>對議定書有效性進行第五次評估與審查之結果，<sup>49</sup></p>","en":[5]},{"md":"**亦注意到**許多締約方在確保參與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之實驗室設施永續運作、維護與持續發展方面所面臨的挑戰，以及締約方之間持續存在的技術與制度能力之顯著差異，","html":"<p><strong>亦注意到</strong>許多締約方在確保參與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之實驗室設施永續運作、維護與持續發展方面所面臨的挑戰，以及締約方之間持續存在的技術與制度能力之顯著差異，</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"1. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織視情況審查並更新透過生物安全資訊交換所提供之實驗室登記冊中所含資訊，並提名額外之實驗室與專家以參與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網路；","html":"<p>1. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織視情況審查並更新透過生物安全資訊交換所提供之實驗室登記冊中所含資訊，並提名額外之實驗室與專家以參與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網路；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"2. **鼓勵**締約方支持區域性實驗室網路與夥伴關係之建立、振興與強化，以促進基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定領域之能力建構、知識共享與技術合作；","html":"<p>2. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方支持區域性實驗室網路與夥伴關係之建立、振興與強化，以促進基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定領域之能力建構、知識共享與技術合作；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"3. **亦鼓勵**締約方制定長期國家策略，以確保參與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之實驗室設施之永續運作、維護與持續發展，包括透過制度支持與區域合作；","html":"<p>3. <strong>亦鼓勵</strong>締約方制定長期國家策略，以確保參與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之實驗室設施之永續運作、維護與持續發展，包括透過制度支持與區域合作；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"4. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及國際組織提供財務資源，特別是針對開發中國家，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之國家，以強化基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之實驗室基礎設施、技術專業與實驗室品質管制系統；","html":"<p>4. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及國際組織提供財務資源，特別是針對開發中國家，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之國家，以強化基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之實驗室基礎設施、技術專業與實驗室品質管制系統；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"5. **決定**制定關於數位聚合酶連鎖反應之補充章節，以補充《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書架構下基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定訓練手冊》（生物安全技術系列第 5 號）；","html":"<p>5. <strong>決定</strong>制定關於數位聚合酶連鎖反應之補充章節，以補充《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書架構下基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定訓練手冊》（生物安全技術系列第 5 號）；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"6. **請求**執行秘書：","html":"<p>6. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書：</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"(a) 與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網路合作，起草上述第 5 段所述之關於數位聚合酶連鎖反應的補充章節；\n(b) 召開實驗室網路之線上討論，以促進該補充章節之制定與同儕審查，供科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構隨後審議；","html":"<p>(a) 與基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網路合作，起草上述第 5 段所述之關於數位聚合酶連鎖反應的補充章節；<br />\n(b) 召開實驗室網路之線上討論，以促進該補充章節之制定與同儕審查，供科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構隨後審議；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[13]},{"md":"$^{48}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{49}$ 參見 CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1.","html":"<p><sup>48</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>49</sup> 參見 CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1.</p>","en":[14,15,16,17]}]},{"p":"p026","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p026.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"7.    Requests the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice to review the draft supplemental chapter and make a recommendation for consideration by the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol at its thirteenth meeting;"},{"t":"8.     Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources:"},{"t":"(a) To explore ways to strengthen the Network of Laboratories for the Detection and Identification of Living Modified Organisms, including by facilitating the visibility of regional and subregional laboratory networks and related collaborative initiatives and by encouraging the participation of additional laboratories and experts in the Network;"},{"t":"(b) To continue to improve the dedicated portal on the sampling, detection and identification of living modified organisms in the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"(c) To continue to collaborate with relevant organizations in order to provide practical and hands-on training on the detection and identification of living modified organisms to laboratory personnel and to customs and border-control officials."},{"t":"26/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"7. **請求**科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構審閱決議草案補充章節，並提出建議，以供擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會在其第十三屆會議時進行審議；","html":"<p>7. <strong>請求</strong>科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構審閱決議草案補充章節，並提出建議，以供擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會在其第十三屆會議時進行審議；</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"8. **請求**執行秘書，視資源而定：","html":"<p>8. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書，視資源而定：</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(a) 探索強化基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網路之方法，包括透過提升區域與次區域實驗室網路及相關協作倡議的能見度，以及鼓勵更多實驗室與專家參與該網路；\n(b) 繼續改善生物安全資訊交換所中關於基因改造活生物體採樣、偵測與鑑定的專用入口網站；\n(c) 繼續與相關組織合作，為實驗室人員以及海關與邊境管制官員提供關於基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定的實務與動手操作培訓。","html":"<p>(a) 探索強化基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網路之方法，包括透過提升區域與次區域實驗室網路及相關協作倡議的能見度，以及鼓勵更多實驗室與專家參與該網路；<br />\n(b) 繼續改善生物安全資訊交換所中關於基因改造活生物體採樣、偵測與鑑定的專用入口網站；<br />\n(c) 繼續與相關組織合作，為實驗室人員以及海關與邊境管制官員提供關於基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定的實務與動手操作培訓。</p>","en":[3,4,5,6]}]},{"p":"p027","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p027.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 15"},{"t":"Socioeconomic considerations"},{"t":"The following decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/11."},{"t":"Socioeconomic considerations"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"1.    Welcomes the information shared on experiences in the use of the guidance on the assessment of socioeconomic considerations in the context of Article 26 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,50,51 while recognizing that limited information was submitted;"},{"t":"2.    Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to continue to share experiences on socioeconomic considerations, including the use of the guidance, in the Biosafety Clearing-House virtual library, as well as through the sixth national reports;"},{"t":"3.    Requests the Executive Secretary to prepare an overview of the information shared pursuant to paragraph 2 above to the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety, at its fourteenth meeting."},{"t":"50 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"51 CBD/CP/MOP/9/10, annex."},{"t":"27/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 15\n社會經濟考量\n以下決議係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/11。","html":"<p>項目 15<br />\n社會經濟考量<br />\n以下決議係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/11。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"社會經濟考量\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會\n1. **歡迎**針對在卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第 26 條脈絡下，使用社會經濟考量評估指南之經驗所分享的資訊，$^{50,51}$ 並同時注意到提交的資訊有限；\n2. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織持續透過生物安全資訊交換所虛擬圖書館以及第六次國家報告，分享關於社會經濟考量的經驗，包括指南的使用；\n3. **請求**執行秘書針對依據上述第 2 段所分享之資訊，準備一份概覽，提交擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第十四屆會議。","html":"<p>社會經濟考量<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會<br />\n1. <strong>歡迎</strong>針對在卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第 26 條脈絡下，使用社會經濟考量評估指南之經驗所分享的資訊，$^{50,51}$ 並同時注意到提交的資訊有限；<br />\n2. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織持續透過生物安全資訊交換所虛擬圖書館以及第六次國家報告，分享關於社會經濟考量的經驗，包括指南的使用；<br />\n3. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書針對依據上述第 2 段所分享之資訊，準備一份概覽，提交擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會第十四屆會議。</p>","en":[4,5,6,7,8]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"$^{50}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{51}$ 參見 CBD/CP/MOP/9/10，附件。","html":"<p><sup>50</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>51</sup> 參見 CBD/CP/MOP/9/10，附件。</p>","en":[9,10,11]}]},{"p":"p028","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p028.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 16"},{"t":"National legislation, regulations and guidelines"},{"t":"on new developments in modern biotechnology"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from document CBD/CP/MOP/12/12."},{"t":"Information on national legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern biotechnology"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"1.     Welcomes the information submitted by Parties regarding current national legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern biotechnology;"},{"t":"2.     Takes note of the information regarding current national legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern biotechnology available through the Biosafety Clearing- House and in other sources, and acknowledges the ongoing efforts in various forums to track information on the development of legislation, regulations and guidelines concerning organisms developed through biotechnology;"},{"t":"3.    Recognizes that modern biotechnology is developing rapidly and that regulatory responses have been developed or are under development in several countries;"},{"t":"4.     Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to submit further information regarding national legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern biotechnology that are relevant to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,52 recognizing the usefulness of exchanging information to build understanding on ongoing developments in relation to legislation, regulations and guidelines and on new developments in modern biotechnology;"},{"t":"5.    Requests the Executive Secretary to prepare an overview of the information submitted in response to the invitation contained in paragraph 4 above, for consideration at its thirteenth meeting."},{"t":"52 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"28/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 16\n現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南\n以下決議草案轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/12。","html":"<p>項目 16<br />\n現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南<br />\n以下決議草案轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/12。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南資訊\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會","html":"<p>關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南資訊<br />\n擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會</p>","en":[5,6]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**締約方就現代生物技術新發展之現行國家立法、法規與指南所提交之資訊；\n2. **注意到**透過生物安全資訊交換所及其他來源可取得關於現代生物技術新發展之現行國家立法、法規與指南資訊，並**承認**各論壇在追蹤與生物技術開發之生物體相關立法、法規與指南發展資訊方面所持續進行之努力；\n3. **認可**現代生物技術正迅速發展，且若干國家已制定或正在制定監管應對措施；\n4. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織提交與卡塔赫納生物安全議定書相關之現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南之進一步資訊，$^{52}$ 並**認可**交換資訊對於增進對立法、法規與指南之持續發展以及現代生物技術新發展之理解具有用處；\n5. **請求**執行秘書針對回應上述第 4 段邀請所提交之資訊編製一份概覽，以供其第十三屆會議審議。","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>締約方就現代生物技術新發展之現行國家立法、法規與指南所提交之資訊；<br />\n2. <strong>注意到</strong>透過生物安全資訊交換所及其他來源可取得關於現代生物技術新發展之現行國家立法、法規與指南資訊，並<strong>承認</strong>各論壇在追蹤與生物技術開發之生物體相關立法、法規與指南發展資訊方面所持續進行之努力；<br />\n3. <strong>認可</strong>現代生物技術正迅速發展，且若干國家已制定或正在制定監管應對措施；<br />\n4. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織提交與卡塔赫納生物安全議定書相關之現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南之進一步資訊，<sup>52</sup> 並<strong>認可</strong>交換資訊對於增進對立法、法規與指南之持續發展以及現代生物技術新發展之理解具有用處；<br />\n5. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書針對回應上述第 4 段邀請所提交之資訊編製一份概覽，以供其第十三屆會議審議。</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"$^{52}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p><sup>52</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[12,13]}]},{"p":"p029","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p029.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Item 17"},{"t":"Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress"},{"t":"The following draft decision has been reproduced from CBD/CP/MOP/12/13."},{"t":"Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol and further serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol,53"},{"t":"Recalling Article 13 of the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,54"},{"t":"Recalling also Goal A.10 of the implementation plan55 and the capacity-building action plan56 for the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety,57"},{"t":"Taking note of the information provided for the first assessment and review of the Nagoya- Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol,"},{"t":"1.    Welcomes the additional instrument of accession to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety that has been deposited since the adoption of decision CP-11/10 of 25 October 2024;"},{"t":"2.   Invites all Parties to the Cartagena Protocol that have not yet done so to deposit an instrument of ratification, acceptance, approval or accession to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol as soon as possible;"},{"t":"3.     Welcomes the fact that almost all Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol have reported the designation of a competent authority to perform the functions set out in Article 5 of the Supplementary Protocol, but expresses concern that relatively few Parties have made information on such authorities available through the Biosafety Clearing-House, and encourages Parties to update and maintain information on their competent authorities on the Biosafety Clearing- House;"},{"t":"4.    Welcomes the information related to the implementation of the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol provided by Parties thereto and by other Governments in their fifth national reports under the Cartagena Protocol, which has informed the first assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Supplementary Protocol;"},{"t":"5.     Also welcomes the steps taken by Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol towards its implementation, while recognizing that there are areas where implementation needs to be strengthened;"},{"t":"6.   Recognizes that financial security measures relating to damage, as defined in the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol, remain limited among Parties thereto;"},{"t":"53 In accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 14 of the Supplementary Protocol, and subject to paragraph 2 of Article 32 of the"},{"t":"Convention on Biological Diversity, the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol serves as the meeting of the Parties to the Supplementary Protocol. Consequently, the present decision has been adopted by the Parties to the Supplementary Protocol."},{"t":"54 Decision BS-V/11, annex."},{"t":"55 Decision CP-10/3, annex."},{"t":"56 Decision CP-10/4, annex."},{"t":"57 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"29/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 17\n名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書\n以下決議草案係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/13。","html":"<p>項目 17<br />\n名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書<br />\n以下決議草案係轉錄自文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/13。</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書\n同時作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議，且進一步作為名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，$^{53}$","html":"<p>名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書<br />\n同時作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議，且進一步作為名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，<sup>53</sup></p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"**回顧**《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書》第 13 條，$^{54}$","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書》第 13 條，<sup>54</sup></p>","en":[6]},{"md":"**亦回顧**《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書執行計畫》之長期目標 A.10 $^{55}$ 以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書能力建構行動計畫》$^{56}$，$^{57}$","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書執行計畫》之長期目標 A.10 <sup>55</sup> 以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書能力建構行動計畫》<sup>56</sup>，<sup>57</sup></p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**注意到**為進行名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書第一次評估與審查所提供的資訊，","html":"<p><strong>注意到</strong>為進行名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書第一次評估與審查所提供的資訊，</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**自 2024 年 10 月 25 日決議 CP-11/10 通過以來，已交存之關於《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書》之額外加入文書；","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>自 2024 年 10 月 25 日決議 CP-11/10 通過以來，已交存之關於《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書》之額外加入文書；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"2. **邀請**尚未這樣做之所有卡塔赫納議定書締約方，盡快交存對名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書之批准、接受、核准或加入文書；","html":"<p>2. <strong>邀請</strong>尚未這樣做之所有卡塔赫納議定書締約方，盡快交存對名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書之批准、接受、核准或加入文書；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"3. **歡迎**幾乎所有名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書締約方皆已通報指定國家主管機關以履行補充議定書第 5 條所規定之職能，但**表示關切**相對較少締約方透過生物安全資訊交換所提供此類主管機關之資訊，並**鼓勵**締約方於生物安全資訊交換所更新並維護其國家主管機關之資訊；","html":"<p>3. <strong>歡迎</strong>幾乎所有名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書締約方皆已通報指定國家主管機關以履行補充議定書第 5 條所規定之職能，但<strong>表示關切</strong>相對較少締約方透過生物安全資訊交換所提供此類主管機關之資訊，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方於生物安全資訊交換所更新並維護其國家主管機關之資訊；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"4. **歡迎**名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書締約方及其他政府在其《卡塔赫納議定書第五次國家報告》中提供之與執行名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書相關之資訊，該資訊已為補充議定書有效性之第一次評估與審查提供了依據；","html":"<p>4. <strong>歡迎</strong>名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書締約方及其他政府在其《卡塔赫納議定書第五次國家報告》中提供之與執行名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書相關之資訊，該資訊已為補充議定書有效性之第一次評估與審查提供了依據；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"5. **亦歡迎**名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書締約方為推動其執行所採取之步驟，同時**承認**在某些領域仍需加強執行；","html":"<p>5. <strong>亦歡迎</strong>名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書締約方為推動其執行所採取之步驟，同時<strong>承認</strong>在某些領域仍需加強執行；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"6. **承認**在該補充議定書締約方中，關於如名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書所定義之損害相關財務保障措施仍然有限；","html":"<p>6. <strong>承認</strong>在該補充議定書締約方中，關於如名古屋－吉隆坡補充議定書所定義之損害相關財務保障措施仍然有限；</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[14]},{"md":"$^{53}$ 根據補充議定書第 14 條第 1 段，且在符合《生物多樣性公約》第 32 條第 2 段之前提下，作為議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，即為補充議定書締約方會議。因此，本決議係由補充議定書締約方所通過。\n$^{54}$ 決議 BS-V/11，附件。\n$^{55}$ 決議 CP-10/3，附件。\n$^{56}$ 決議 CP-10/4，附件。\n$^{57}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p><sup>53</sup> 根據補充議定書第 14 條第 1 段，且在符合《生物多樣性公約》第 32 條第 2 段之前提下，作為議定書締約方會議之締約方大會，即為補充議定書締約方會議。因此，本決議係由補充議定書締約方所通過。<br />\n<sup>54</sup> 決議 BS-V/11，附件。<br />\n<sup>55</sup> 決議 CP-10/3，附件。<br />\n<sup>56</sup> 決議 CP-10/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>57</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[15,16,17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p030","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p030.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"7.     Also recognizes that many Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol rely on environmental, administrative or civil liability frameworks to address liability for damage resulting from living modified organisms;"},{"t":"8.     Encourages Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol to develop or facilitate access to financial security, in accordance with Article 10 thereof, and develop or apply civil liability rules and procedures addressing damage, in accordance with Article 12;"},{"t":"9.     Also encourages Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol to continue efforts towards the full implementation of the Supplementary Protocol;"},{"t":"10. Invites Parties and other Governments to publish information on developments related to the implementation of the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol through the virtual library of the Biosafety Clearing-House, with a view to sharing experiences in that regard;"},{"t":"11. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations to continue to support capacity-building activities in support of the effective implementation of the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol, and encourages donors to provide the necessary resources in that regard, with a view to meeting Goal A.10 of the implementation plan and the capacity-building action plan for the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"12. Requests the Executive Secretary to follow up with Parties to the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol that have reported the designation of a competent authority but that have not yet published its contact details through the Biosafety Clearing-House;"},{"t":"13. Also requests the Executive Secretary to continue to promote the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol, with a view to supporting its ratification, and, subject to the availability to resources, undertake outreach and awareness-raising activities in relation to the Supplementary Protocol."},{"t":"30/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"7. 亦認可名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之許多締約方，依賴環境、行政或民事責任框架，以處理因基因改造活生物體所造成損害之責任；\n8. **鼓勵**名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之締約方，根據該議定書第 10 條，開發或促進取得財務保障之管道，並根據第 12 條，開發或適用處理損害之民事責任規則與程序；\n9. 亦**鼓勵**名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之締約方，持續致力於充分落實該補充議定書；\n10. **邀請**締約方與其他政府，透過生物安全資訊交換所之虛擬圖書館，發布與落實名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書相關進展之資訊，以期分享該方面之經驗；\n11. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織，持續支持有助於有效落實名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之能力建構活動，並**鼓勵**捐助者就此提供必要資源，以期達成卡塔赫納生物安全議定書落實計畫與能力建構行動計畫之長期目標 A.10；\n12. **請求**執行秘書追蹤已通報指定國家主管機關，但尚未透過生物安全資訊交換所公布其聯絡詳情之名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書締約方；\n13. 亦**請求**執行秘書持續推廣名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書，以支持其批准，並視資源而定，開展與該補充議定書相關的推廣與提升意識活動。","html":"<p>7. 亦認可名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之許多締約方，依賴環境、行政或民事責任框架，以處理因基因改造活生物體所造成損害之責任；<br />\n8. <strong>鼓勵</strong>名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之締約方，根據該議定書第 10 條，開發或促進取得財務保障之管道，並根據第 12 條，開發或適用處理損害之民事責任規則與程序；<br />\n9. 亦<strong>鼓勵</strong>名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之締約方，持續致力於充分落實該補充議定書；<br />\n10. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方與其他政府，透過生物安全資訊交換所之虛擬圖書館，發布與落實名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書相關進展之資訊，以期分享該方面之經驗；<br />\n11. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織，持續支持有助於有效落實名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之能力建構活動，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>捐助者就此提供必要資源，以期達成卡塔赫納生物安全議定書落實計畫與能力建構行動計畫之長期目標 A.10；<br />\n12. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書追蹤已通報指定國家主管機關，但尚未透過生物安全資訊交換所公布其聯絡詳情之名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書締約方；<br />\n13. 亦<strong>請求</strong>執行秘書持續推廣名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書，以支持其批准，並視資源而定，開展與該補充議定書相關的推廣與提升意識活動。</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]}]},{"p":"p031","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6aba80c6bb45afc8bbd1cd96/p031.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/CP/MOP/12/2"},{"t":"Items 18 to 20"},{"t":"No draft decisions are envisaged under items 18 to 20, owing to the nature of those items. The actions required on the part of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Protocol under those items are reflected in the annotated provisional agenda."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"31/31"}],"blocks":[{"md":"項目 18 至 20","html":"<p>項目 18 至 20</p>","pre":"","dup":true,"en":[0,1]},{"md":"由於這些項目之性質，預計在項目 18 至 20 下不設決議草案。擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會根據這些項目所需採取之行動，已反映於附註臨時議程中。\n__________","html":"<p>由於這些項目之性質，預計在項目 18 至 20 下不設決議草案。擔任議定書締約方會議之締約方大會根據這些項目所需採取之行動，已反映於附註臨時議程中。</p>\n<hr />","en":[2,3,4]}]}]};
